    'SAIC', 'https://serpapi.com/searches/6ab37566304ebad94a0c3ec6/images/skYUYTRMtYqJz6mPAZOa7ujT0QqQRN-bN2fUmZMu93s.jpeg', 'Software Developer', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Job ID: 2615838

Location: Remote Work, TN, US

Date Posted: 2026-08-26

Category: Software

Subcategory: SW Engineer

Schedule: Full-Time

Shift: Day Job

Travel: Yes - 10% of the time

Minimum Clearance Required: None

Clearance Level Must Be Able to Obtain: Secret

Potential for Remote Work: ORA_REMOTE
 
Description 
 
SAIC''s STG is seeking a talented and motivated Mid-Level Software Developer to join our growing team focused on the design, development, and deployment of a next-generation Agentic AI Platform. In this role, you will contribute to building intelligent, autonomous agent frameworks and modern web applications that support complex decision-making workflows. You will work across the full development stack - from crafting intuitive front-end user experiences to building robust backend services and cloud infrastructure components. This role can be worked remotely anywhere in the United States. Candidates must have the ability to get a secret clearance. 

Responsibilities


Design, develop, and maintain front-end web applications using modern web technologies and low-code platformsBuild and style responsive, user-friendly interfaces within the Mendix platform, ensuring a polished and effective user experienceDevelop and maintain backend REST services and business logic to support platform capabilities and agentic AI workflowsContribute to the development of agentic AI components, including integration with frameworks such as LangChain, LangGraph, and LangSmithSupport development and deployment of cloud-based services and infrastructure on AWS, leveraging tools such as OpenSearch, SageMaker, Lambda, and SQSDevelop and maintain Infrastructure as Code (IaC) using tools such as Terraform, Packer, and TerragruntCollaborate with AI/ML engineers, architects, and product owners to translate requirements into scalable, production-ready solutionsSupport testing, debugging, and performance optimization of platform componentsMaintain documentation for system architecture, APIs, and development processes 

Qualifications 
 Bachelor''s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field and 2 years of experience. Masters and 0 years2-5 years of professional software development experienceExperience building front-end web applications using core web technologies: HTML, CSS, and JavaScriptExperience developing backend services and APIs, including RESTful service design and complex business logic implementation, using languages such as Python, Java, or NodeJSStrong problem-solving skills and ability to work effectively in a fast-paced, collaborative agile environmentPass CompTIA Security Plus Examination within 90 Days of EmploymentCandidates must have the ability to get a secret clearance
Preferred Qualifications
Experience with HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and ReactJS for building modern, component-based web applications. Familiarity with low-code development platforms, particularly Mendix (note: team training on Mendix is provided). Ability to effectively style and design front-end applications for usability and visual consistencyPython development experience, particularly for backend service development. Hands-on experience with Agentic AI frameworks such as LangChain, LangGraph, and/or LangSmith. Familiarity with multi-agent orchestration, autonomous workflow design, or LLM integration patternsExperience with AWS cloud services, including one or more of the following: OpenSearch, SageMaker, Lambda, SQSExperience with Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tools, including: Terraform, Packer, TerragruntFamiliarity with DevSecOps practices 
 
 Target salary range: $80,001 - $120,000. The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position based on experience and other factors.',
    'active', '2026-09-23T06:51:23.438189+00:00', '', 'google_jobs', 'https://www.dice.com/job-detail/e8387da2-4e46-4887-bf75-2a269291c41c', TRUE, ARRAY['Software Engineer','Remote']::TEXT[]
)
