) VALUES (
    'Reddit', 'https://serpapi.com/searches/6ab37579f5d5ac8e436e519f/images/Pd2ux4bZpFTJO5OtuC96EZDmCdLizMhXkfwgNAnfbV4.jpeg', 'Front End Software Engineer, Consumer Engineering', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Reddit is a community of communities. It''s built on shared interests, passion, and trust, and is home to the most open and authentic conversations on the internet. Every day, Reddit users submit, vote, and comment on the topics they care most about. With 100,000+ active communities and approximately 130 million daily active unique visitors, Reddit is one of the internet''s largest sources of information. For more information, visit www.redditinc.com.




The Reddit Consumer Engineering organization builds and scales the products that Redditors use directly to discover content, participate in communities, and connect with others. Sitting at the intersection of large-scale distributed systems and core user journeys, Product Engineers in Consumer Engineering partner directly with Product Managers, Designers, Data Scientists, ML Engineers, and Frontend Engineers to build, experiment with, and scale features that power how hundreds of millions of users discover, join, navigate, and engage with Reddit.




This centralized role hires across several high-impact consumer teams, including:





 Core Product & Feeds: Home Experience, Recommendations & Content Discovery, Content Contribution
 Community & Presence: Reddit Pro, Youth Experience & Teen Safety, Creator Tools
 Growth & Engagement: Authentication, Notifications, Social Sharing, SEO, Onboarding.
 Monetization & Conversion: Paid User Acquisition, Conversion Funnel Optimization
 Identity & Security: Account Management, Trust & Safety
What You''ll Do



 Cross-Functional Product Architecture: Partner closely with Product Management, Product Design, Data Science, and Client Engineers (iOS/Android/Web) to translate business and user needs into reliable, low-latency technical solutions.
 End-to-End Delivery: Own the full software lifecycle for major product initiatives from technical design docs and API contracts to development, testing, rollout, and observability.
 Metrics & Experimentation-Led Engineering: Design, build, and evaluate A/B experiments. Work with tools like BigQuery, HEX, or Firebase to analyze user behavior, conversion funnels, and retention loops to make data-backed engineering decisions.
 API & System Performance: Build and maintain scalable APIs (GraphQL, REST, gRPC) and distributed backend services optimized for client consumption and consumer UI performance.
 Technical Rigor & Modern Tooling: Establish engineering best practices, improve developer workflows, mentor teammates, and use modern, AI-integrated tools to ship high-quality products efficiently.
Who You Are



 User-Centric Mindset: An advocate for the user with an intuitive feel for product usability, interaction design, social dynamics, and user growth loops. You care deeply about why a feature is being built and its impact on the end user.
 Data-Informed & Hypothesis-Driven: Comfortable working alongside Data Scientists and PMs to design experiments, establish core performance metrics, and iterate quickly based on real-time feedback.
 Technical Rigor at Scale: 5+ years of hands-on backend development experience building and operating large-scale distributed serving systems in high-concurrency environments.
 Bias for Action: Self-directed, innovative, and comfortable navigating ambiguity in fast-paced product environments where balancing velocity with system reliability is essential.
 Collaborative Communicator: Outstanding communication skills with a track record of driving cross-functional alignment in fully remote or hybrid team environments.
Technical Qualifications



 Languages: Proficiency in one or more front end focused programming languages: Javascript, Typescript, ES6
 Experience with one or more front-end web frameworks such as LIT, Polymer, React, Vue, or Angular with experience with CSS.
 Modern Workflows: Experience or interest in using AI-assisted engineering tools to accelerate development workflows.


Benefits:



 Comprehensive Healthcare Benefits and Income Replacement Programs
 401k with Employer Match
 Global Benefit programs that fit your lifestyle, from workspace to professional development to caregiving support
 Family Planning Support
 Gender-Affirming Care
 Mental Health & Coaching Benefits
 Flexible Vacation & Paid Volunteer Time Off
 Generous Paid Parental Leave



#LI-remote



Pay Transparency:




This job posting may span more than one career level.




In addition to base salary, this job is eligible to receive equity in the form of restricted stock units, and depending on the position offered, it may also be eligible to receive a commission. Additionally, Reddit offers a wide range of benefits to U.S.-based employees, including medical, dental, and vision insurance, 401(k) program with employer match, generous time off for vacation, and parental leave. To learn more, please visit https://www.redditinc.com/careers/.




To provide greater transparency to candidates, we share base salary ranges for all US-based job postings regardless of state. We set standard base pay ranges for all roles based on function, level, and country location, benchmarked against similar stage growth companies. Final offer amounts are determined by multiple factors including, skills, depth of work experience and relevant licenses/credentials, and may vary from the amounts listed below.




The base salary range for this position is:




$164,200-$229,900 USD




In select roles and locations, the interviews will be recorded, transcribed and summarized by artificial intelligence (AI). You will have the opportunity to opt out of recording, transcription and summarization prior to any scheduled interviews.




During the interview, we will collect the following categories of personal information: Identifiers, Professional and Employment-Related Information, Sensory Information (audio/video recording), and any other categories of personal information you choose to share with us. We will use this information to evaluate your application for employment or an independent contractor role, as applicable. We will not sell your personal information or disclose it to any third party for their marketing purposes. We will delete any recording of your interview promptly after making a hiring decision. For more information about how we will handle your personal information, including our retention of it, please refer to our Candidate Privacy Policy for Potential Employees and Contractors.




Reddit is proud to be an equal opportunity employer, and is committed to building a workforce representative of the diverse communities we serve. Reddit is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities and disabled veterans in our job application procedures. If, due to a disability, you need an accommodation during the interview process, please let your recruiter know.',
    'active', '2026-09-17T06:51:23.439796+00:00', '', 'google_jobs', 'https://www.ziprecruiter.com/c/reddit/Job/Front-End-Software-Engineer,-Consumer-Engineering/-in-Remote,US?jid=cd7d383d76a2c20d', TRUE, ARRAY['Frontend Engineer','Remote']::TEXT[]
)
