    'remote quest jobs', NULL, '[Remote] Frontend Engineer, Device OS', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Note: The job is a remote job and is open to candidates in USA. reputed company is a company focused on developing custom hardware appliances and software platforms. They are seeking an experienced Frontend Engineer to design and maintain applications that improve the performance and user experience of their Device OS platform. The role involves collaborating with cross-functional teams to ensure the front-end architecture is efficient and responsive, ultimately enhancing how customers interact with their appliances.


Responsibilities

Design, build, and maintain React and TypeScript applications where customers see how their appliances are performing and configure them, and that expose device workflows, telemetry, and control surfaces to field operators, partners, and internal teamsCare deeply about performance — partner with backend engineers to shape the data that flows to the front end so pages and apps load fast and stay responsive under real operational loadWork hand-in-hand with design to craft the best possible customer experience, contributing to UX decisions rather than just implementing themOwn the front-end architecture — component structure, state management, and data-fetching patterns — keeping the codebase maintainable, testable, and scalable as the platform growsBuild responsive, accessible interfaces that hold up under real operational conditions: large data sets, real-time updates, and intermittent connectivity at partner sitesIntegrate deeply with RESTful APIs and real-time data streams, handling asynchronous state, loading and error conditions, and graceful failure with careTranslate complex device states and workflows into clear, intuitive UI that makes correctness, status, and next actions obvious to the operatorBuild and extend shared component libraries and design systems so the team ships consistent, high-quality UI quicklyCollaborate cross-functionally with backend, hardware, and field operations teams to deliver complete, field-ready featuresConduct thorough code reviews, write technical design documents, and raise the engineering bar across the teamBuild and extend our Tailwind CSS–based design system and shared component packages so multiple apps across the platform ship consistent UI
Skills

