    'Motion Recruitment', 'https://serpapi.com/searches/6ab37584998aad3f994a8d11/images/f0gWkUqCaERjce5Yn7UToELY9QD-baI4mA3fts2QgJk.jpeg', 'Remote Frontend Engineer / React / WebGL / 3D', 'Remote', 'Contractor',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'A growing sports technology company is seeking a full-time WebGL Front End Developer to help build next-generation race tracking and analytics products. This position focuses on creating highly interactive visualization experiences using TypeScript, modern frontend frameworks, and advanced browser rendering technologies. Engineers will work on applications that process real-time telemetry and geospatial data, transforming complex information into intuitive user experiences for athletes and coaches.


This opportunity is ideal for developers who enjoy solving performance-intensive frontend challenges. Rather than building traditional business applications, this engineer will help create immersive replay systems, live tracking platforms, and analytics tools that resemble simulation and gaming experiences. The organization values engineers who can take ownership of their work, propose architectural improvements, and collaborate closely across product and backend teams.


Contract Duration: 6 – 12 Months


Required Skills & Experience



5+ years of professional software engineering experience
Strong experience with TypeScript and modern frontend frameworks including React, Vue, or Svelte
Hands-on experience with WebGL, Three.js, WebGPU, Canvas, deck.gl, or similar technologies
Experience building data visualization applications
Understanding of WebSockets, real-time streaming, and event-driven systems
Ability to analyze and optimize application performance
Experience developing consumer-facing products

Desired Skills & Experience

Sports analytics or telemetry experience
Geospatial data visualization experience
Gaming, simulation, rendering, or VFX backgrounds
Timeline and replay system development experience
AI-powered product development experience
Flutter or Dart exposure
Go experience
Experience working with large-scale time-series datasets
Interest in performance analytics and sports technology

What You Will Be Doing
Tech Breakdown

60% TypeScript / Frontend Development
20% Graphics Rendering & Visualization
10% Real-Time Data Systems
10% Performance Optimization

Daily Responsibilities

80% Hands On Development
5% Management Duties
15% Team Collaboration

