    status, posted_at, external_id, source, url, is_remote, tags
) VALUES (
    'ClickUp', 'https://serpapi.com/searches/6ab37586304ebae0c2fc46f6/images/uAI6O7LHUTZR7rKCUBwB7UkNjN0jGnOF9n_XXeuKbZ0.jpeg', 'Senior Frontend Engineer, Docs', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'At ClickUp, we’re not just building software. We’re architecting the future of work! In a world overwhelmed by work sprawl, we saw a better way. That’s why we created the first truly converged AI workspace, unifying tasks, docs, chat, calendar, and enterprise search, all supercharged by context-driven AI, empowering millions of teams to break free from silos, reclaim their time, and unlock new levels of productivity. At ClickUp, you’ll have the opportunity to learn, use, and pioneer AI in ways that shape not only our product, but the future of work itself. Join us and be part of a bold, innovative team that’s redefining what’s possible! 🚀

About the Role
At ClickUp, files and media are foundational to how work gets done. From design proofs and video clips to project specs and legal documents, these assets are deeply integrated into every surface of our product. Our success depends on making these interactions seamless, secure, and incredibly fast.
 
We are looking for a Senior Frontend Engineer to own the user experience for all file interactions. This is a commitment to performance and user experience at scale. You will be responsible for ensuring that working with files in ClickUp feels instantaneous and intuitive, whether it''s a small team uploading an avatar or an enterprise customer streaming high-resolution video. Your work will directly impact millions of users every day and is critical to our success as we expand our customer footprint.
What You’ll Do

Own and deliver a world-class user experience for all file interactions, from ergonomic uploads with clear, asynchronous feedback to high-performance media previews.
Architect and implement highly observable, scalable, and resilient frontend systems for file management using Angular, NgRx, and reactive programming patterns.
Dive deep into performance bottlenecks, using user-centric metrics to eliminate latency and ensure reliable, large-scale content delivery.
Collaborate across the full system, cooperatively debugging issues from the browser, through our delivery pipeline (CDNs, Lambdas), to our NodeJS services. You''ll join a global on-call rotation with your team for the systems you collectively own.
Mentor other engineers and support best practices in frontend architecture. You''ll help create a stable environment for deep work by driving thoughtful planning and clear, pragmatic roadmaps.

Who You Are

You are a pragmatic, hands-on engineer who thrives on cooperatively solving complex frontend needs and has a proven track record of shipping focused, end-to-end projects.
You have deep expertise in a modern frontend framework (like Angular or React) and a strong command of reactive programming and state management patterns.
You have an obsession with performance and observability. You don''t just fix bugs; you instrument, measure, and understand user-centric metrics to drive lasting, systemic improvements.
You are not afraid to cross boundaries. You see the full delivery stack—from S3 and Lambda to the browser—not as a black box, but as part of the system you are responsible for improving.
You consistently solve problems that others can''t and act as a support multiplier for the team you work with.
You justify your technical understandings with data and clear reasoning, delivering solutions that are secure, performant, and maintainable.

#LI-Remote


#LI-RL1

Salary and Benefits


At ClickUp, we believe in transparency and fairness in compensation. The range displayed reflects the minimum and maximum target salaries for the position across all US locations. Please note that the actual compensation for this position may vary and is dependent on factors such as geographic location,  interview performance, years of experience, education level, and specific skills. We encourage candidates to discuss compensation expectations during the interview process to ensure alignment with their qualifications and our company’s compensation philosophy.


This position is eligible for the following benefits and perks:



 Equity
 401k
 Health, Dental, and Vision insurance
 Spending accounts
 Life & Disability
 Paid parental leave
 Flexible paid time off
 Enhanced employee assistance program
 Employee wellness stipend
 Professional development stipend
USA Salary Range (OTE)$160,000—$205,000 USD 



Unsure if you meet all the qualifications of this job description but are deeply excited about the role? We hire based on ambition, grit, and a passion for improving the way people work. If you think ClickUp is the company for you, we encourage you to apply!


At ClickUp, we assess every candidate based on the potential impact they can have. We hire the best people for the job and support each person’s journey to build their boldest career.
 
ClickUp is an Equal Opportunity Employer, and qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin.

ClickUp collects and processes personal data in accordance with applicable data protection laws.



If you are a European Job Applicant, see our privacy policy for further details.
If you are a Philippine Job Applicant, see our privacy policy and our Philippine Data Privacy Notice for further details. 

Please note we are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa for roles outside of engineering and product at this time. Sponsorship for engineering and product roles is not guaranteed, but is instead based on the business needs for that specific role at that time. Please reach out to the recruiter with any questions.



ClickUp Talent Acquisition will only initiate contact via an @clickup.com email or through our official careers portal on clickup.com. We will never request fees, payments, or sensitive personal information. Please disregard any offers received outside these channels and report them to support@clickup.com.',
    'active', '2026-09-23T06:51:23.440620+00:00', '', 'google_jobs', 'https://applyall.com/jobs/us/senior-frontend-engineer-docs-at-clickup-jc_pwZvQhjswc8cul6eKh9gJMvH', TRUE, ARRAY['Frontend Engineer','Remote']::TEXT[]
)
