    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'About OpenTrainOpenTrain is the #1 platform for finding and building careers in AI training and data labeling. OpenTrain AI is recruiting for this contract opportunity and helps professionals discover projects, build a credible profile, and grow their experience in a fast-moving technology industry.

Remote contract work available across many countriesPart-time schedule of 20+ hours per weekHourly compensation from $30 to $80 USDAbout AI Training WorkAI training is the human side of building modern artificial intelligence. Contributors use professional expertise to prepare, review, and evaluate the examples that help AI systems become more useful, reliable, and aligned with real-world needs.

Frontend professionals can contribute by applying practical judgment about usability, accessibility, performance, and interface quality to work supporting next-generation AI systems.

Work remotely with a computer and internet connectionHelp shape how cutting-edge AI systems are developedUse specialized professional skills in a growing technology fieldThe RoleOpenTrain AI is seeking a contract Frontend UI Engineer to create polished, usable, and accessible interfaces across platforms and devices. This role combines hands-on frontend development with thoughtful review of interface quality, performance, consistency, and end-user experience.

You will translate product needs into responsive experiences while collaborating with product, design, and backend partners. The role is listed at entry level, with demonstrated expertise in UI design principles and frontend development required.

Employment type: Contract, part timeTime requirement: 20+ hours per weekPay range: $30 to $80 USD per hourPrimary language: EnglishWork arrangement: Fully remoteWhat You''ll DoYou will build high-quality interfaces and contribute to the consistency and usability of the products you support. Clear documentation and constructive collaboration are important parts of the work.

Design and develop user interfaces with strong usability and accessibilityTranslate requirements into elegant, functional UI solutionsBuild responsive experiences for cross-platform and cross-device useApply component reuse and frontend performance best practicesParticipate in design reviews and give constructive feedback on UI qualityDocument technical decisions for technical and non-technical stakeholdersTrack relevant UI technologies and apply contemporary development practicesRequired SkillsApplicants should bring strong frontend fundamentals, careful attention to detail, and the ability to communicate technical decisions clearly. Pixel-level execution and empathy for end users are central to the role.

Demonstrated expertise in UI design principles and frontend developmentHands-on experience with React, Vue, Angular, or another modern frontend frameworkStrong command of HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and component-based architecturePractical judgment around accessibility, responsive design, usability, and performanceStrong written and verbal communication skillsAbility to work independently in a fully remote, distributed environmentAbility to explain technical decisions to technical and non-technical collaboratorsHelpful BackgroundExperience with UI animation, micro-interactions, design systems, accessible digital products, inclusive design, or cross-functional remote teams is helpful. Familiarity with the wider AI training context is not required, making this an opportunity for frontend professionals to contribute their domain expertise to AI work.

UI animation or micro-interaction experienceExperience with design systemsBackground building accessible or inclusive digital productsExperience collaborating with cross-functional remote teamsHow It WorksCreate a free OpenTrain account to build your professional profile and apply for this opportunity. OpenTrain helps you present relevant experience and grow a durable portfolio as you take on AI training and data-labeling work.

Create or update your OpenTrain profileHighlight your frontend, UI, accessibility, and performance expertiseApply through OpenTrainBuild experience in the growing AI training industry',
