) VALUES (
    'General Dynamics Information Technology', 'https://serpapi.com/images/i/_9j_4AAQSkZJRgABAQAAAQABAAD_2wCEAAkGBwgHBgkIBwgKCgkLDRYPDQwMDRsUFRAWIB0iIiAdHx8kKDQsJCYxJx8fLT0tMTU3Ojo6Iys_RD84QzQ5OjcBCgoKDQwNGg8PGjclHyU3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3N__AABEIADgAOAMBIgACEQEDEQH_xAAXAAEBAQEAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABwUG_8QAKRAAAQMDAwIFBQAAAAAAAAAAAAECAwQFEQYSIRMiFEGBwdEHFRYkMf_EABUBAQEAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAB_8QAFREBAQAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABH_2gAMAwEAAhEDEQA_ALiAAAAAAAAAAABMtax1LtZvW9x3l9kWhxQ_b-ssaT556iQ92fYCmggjkuq2O-QU1DdGtZNR7J4m1qPmbvXftbKquTCf3HwblbFT-Ltv4NBqZlz8ZHudVJVJAkWe_f1e3GPUsSq-CYaY08-72m-uvjbo2aC61bqX9maFVYu3bjCpubxx5Gj9KbAkOnrdd7glxbdnxvbMlVUS8dypzG5cJwieQV3wAIAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAD_9k.jpeg', 'Full Stack JAVA Developer (Remote)', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    136000, 184000, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Clearance Level 
   
    None
   
  
  
  
   Category 
   
    Software Engineering
   
  
  
  
   Location 
   
    Remote, Working from the USA
   
  
  
  
 
 
  
   Key Skills For Success
  
  
   JasperReports


  
  
   Java Software Development


  
  
   ReAct Framework


  
  
   Test Driven Development (TDD)


  
 
 
 
  
   
    
     
      
      
     
    
    
     REQ#: RQ226668
     Public Trust: Other
     Requisition Type: Regular
     Your Impact
     Own your opportunity to work alongside federal civilian agencies. Make an impact by delivering solutions that improve citizen services millions depends on.


     Job Description
     
      SOFTWARE DEVELOPER SENIOR


      


      We are seeking a Full Stack Java Developer to design and build Java‑based microservices, REST APIs, ingestion pipelines, and reporting solutions. The role includes developing JasperReports, modernizing PACER reporting, writing SQL for data and reconciliation workflows, and executing comprehensive testing across APIs, data pipelines, and reporting outputs. The ideal candidate will support end‑to‑end development, testing, troubleshooting, and collaboration with cross‑functional teams to deliver high‑quality, scalable, and audit‑ready solutions. 

        MEANINGFUL WORK AND PERSONAL IMPACT 

        As a Software Developer Senior, the work you’ll do at GDIT will be impactful to the mission of Bureau of Fiscal Service - Department of Treasury. You will play a crucial role in Modernization of Legacy Applications.



      
       Design and develop Java microservices, REST APIs, and data ingestion pipelines
       Build JasperReports, modernize PACER reports, and implement reconciliation workflows
       Write SQL for data queries, aggregations, and cross‑system data validation
       Execute API, batch, and end‑to‑end testing across ingestion and reporting workflows
       Support troubleshooting, UAT, and collaboration with cross‑functional teams
      
      

      
       

        WHAT YOU’LL NEED TO SUCCEED 
       

        Bring your engineering expertise along with a drive for innovation to GDIT. The Software Developer Senior must have: 
       
        Education: Bachelor Degree in Computers or related field
        Experience: 10+ years of related experience
        Technical skills: Full Stack Java Developer skilled in Java microservices, REST APIs, data ingestion pipelines, SQL, JasperReports, and end‑to‑end testing.
       
      
      
       US citizenship or LPR required
      
      
       Role requirements: Collaborate with Stakeholders, Legacy development team, Business Users, Vendors and interfacing applications
      
      


      Key Responsibilities


      
       Java & Microservices Development
       

       
        Design and develop Java‑based REST APIs and stateless microservices using Javalin
        Build JSON models, validation logic, transformation workflows, and ingestion pipelines (SFTP, batch)
        Integrate with Datacom/CICS systems via JDBC or REST gateways
        Implement structured error handling, logging, and traceability
        Develop unit and integration tests and support troubleshooting across environments
       
      
      
       Reporting & Data Processing
       

       
        Build and maintain JasperReports templates, sub‑reports, and merged outputs
        Modernize PACER reporting, reconciliation logic, and monthly report workflows
        Write SQL for data queries, aggregations, reconciliation checks, and cross‑system data blends
        Automate recurring reporting cycles and generate outputs in CSV, XML, and PDF
       
      
      
       Testing & Quality Assurance
       

       
        Execute unit, integration, API, batch, and end‑to‑end testing
        Validate ingestion formats (Connect:Direct, SFTP, CSV, fixed‑width, XML, JSON)
        Test REST APIs for schema accuracy, error handling, and performance
        Coordinate UAT, lead defect triage, and maintain test documentation and traceability
       
      
      


      
       Required Qualifications
       

       
        10+ years of experience in Java development, microservices, or REST API design
        Hands‑on experience with JSON modeling, data validation, and transformation logic
        Strong SQL skills including joins, aggregations, and reconciliation queries
        Experience building reports using JasperReports or similar reporting frameworks
        Solid understanding of batch processing, SFTP ingestion, or file‑based workflows
        Experience with unit, integration, API, and data‑pipeline testing
        Ability to troubleshoot complex application, data, or report issues across environments
        Strong communication skills and experience working with cross‑functional teams
       
      
      
       Preferred Qualifications
       

       
        Experience with Javalin or other lightweight Java REST frameworks
        Familiarity with PACER reporting, reconciliation processes, or finance‑related data flows
        Prior experience integrating with Datacom/CICS systems via JDBC or REST gateways
        Exposure to Connect:Direct, CSV, fixed‑width, XML, or JSON ingestion pipelines
        Experience with automated scheduling/orchestration tools (e.g., Autosys, Control‑M, Jenkins, etc.)
        Knowledge of logging, traceability, audit frameworks, or compliance‑driven workflows
        Experience supporting UAT or collaborating closely with SMEs in accounting or reporting domains
       
      
      

      
       

        GDIT IS YOUR PLACE 
       

        At GDIT, the mission is our purpose, and our people are at the center of everything we do. 
       
        Growth: AI-powered career tool that identifies career steps and learning opportunities
        Support: An internal mobility team focused on helping you achieve your career goals
        Rewards: Comprehensive benefits and wellness packages, 401K with company match, and competitive pay and paid time off
        Flexibility: Full-flex work week to own your priorities at work and at home ***remove if ineligible***
        Community: Award-winning culture of innovation and a military-friendly workplace
       
       

        OWN YOUR OPPORTUNITY 
       

        Explore a career in software development at GDIT and you’ll find endless opportunities to grow alongside colleagues who share your dedication to advancing innovation.
      
     
    
    
     
      
