    110000, 189000, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Note: The job is a remote job and is open to candidates in USA. LMI is a digital solutions provider supporting government missions through innovative technology and AI solutions. The company is seeking a Full-Stack Developer with Agentic AI to enhance complex software systems, collaborate across multidisciplinary teams, and deliver secure, scalable solutions for customer programs.


Responsibilities

Leverage advanced agentic AI tools to quickly add new functionality into existing code stacks within large, complex programsMake quick, high-impact contributions to strategically critical projects across LMI’s portfolio, ensuring program success and delivering measurable resultsCollaborate with development teams, stakeholders, and technical leads to identify pain points in existing systems and implement solutions in an agile environmentTransition seamlessly between programs, applying technical expertise to prioritize and address the highest-impact initiativesAnalyze customer requirements and program objectives to develop innovative solutions that align with mission needsWork within multidisciplinary teams to facilitate integrations, resolve technical challenges, and adhere to development timelinesEnsure compliance with security protocols, government standards, and industry best practices across all projectsDocument technical solutions and improvements for knowledge transfer between teams and programsConduct rigorous testing to guarantee performance, scalability, and reliability of updated or newly developed code
Skills

**Eligibility for a security clearance is required**: Active Secret clearance preferred3-5 years applying dev in a production environment**Experience with agentic AI coding tools**: Demonstrated proficiency using tools to enhance existing code stacks at scale**Proven full-stack development experience**: Minimum of 3–5 years in developing, maintaining, and improving front-end and back-end systems**Knowledge of programming languages**: Proficient in at least one back-end language (Python preferred) and one front-end framework/tool (TypeScript preferred)**Experience with API development**: Familiarity with developing and consuming RESTful APIs for integration across systems**Familiarity with SQL and NoSQL databases**: Strong foundational skills for managing data within relational (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQL Server) and non-relational (e.g., MongoDB) environments**Agile methodologies**: Experience working in agile environments, including the ability to work collaboratively with multidisciplinary teams**Version control proficiency**: Comfortable using Git (GitLab preferred) for code development and collaboration**Experience with testing, security, DevSecOps, and CI/CD processes**: Proficient in integrating with automated testing frameworks, following security protocols, and following secure, continuous integration/continuous deployment pipelines**Strong communication skills**: Capable of clearly articulating technical concepts and solutions to both technical teams and non-technical stakeholdersApplicants must meet eligibility requirements for a U.S. Government security clearanceOnly US Citizens are eligible for a security clearanceFor this position, LMI will only consider applicants with security clearances or applicants who are eligible for security clearances, due to the nature of the work**Advanced proficiency in agentic AI tools:** Extensive experience utilizing tools to optimize coding workflows and integrate advanced AI functionality**Experience with cloud environments:** Familiarity with AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud for developing and deploying cloud-based applications**Microservices architecture:** Experience in designing and implementing microservices and containerized solutions (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes)**UI/UX design skills:** Knowledge of modern front-end frameworks like React, Vue.js, or Angular to enhance user interface and experience**Knowledge of DevSecOps practices:** Comprehensive understanding of secure development and deployment pipelines, including infrastructure-as-code tools like Terraform or Ansible**Data engineering:** Experience with ETL tools, data pipeline management, and real-time analytics platforms**Security certifications:** Certifications such as Security+ or CISSP are highly desirable**Experience with Agile frameworks:** Advanced knowledge of Agile or SAFe methodologies, including participation in sprint planning and ceremonies
Company Overview

LMI is a consulting firm dedicated to improving the management of government. It was founded in 1961, and is headquartered in Virginia, Nebraska, USA, with a workforce of 1001-5000 employees. Its website is http://www.lmi.org.',
