    status, posted_at, external_id, source, url, is_remote, tags
) VALUES (
    '24-Mag', NULL, 'Remote | DevOps Engineer — $50–$100/hour', 'Remote', 'Contractor',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'We are sharing a specialised consulting opportunity for experienced DevOps, SRE, Platform, and Infrastructure Engineers with strong expertise in Kubernetes, Terraform, CI/CD, Python, Linux, cloud infrastructure, and infrastructure as code to contribute to an advanced AI training and technical evaluation project.


Selected professionals will design realistic DevOps tasks based on production-style scenarios, build working reference solutions, evaluate AI-generated technical outputs, and provide precise corrections grounded in practical infrastructure engineering. The work requires strong coding ability, hands-on cloud and platform experience, and a high standard for correctness and reproducibility. No prior experience in AI is required.


Key Responsibilities


DevOps Scenario & Task Design




Design realistic technical tasks based on production-style DevOps environments


Create scenarios involving CI/CD, containers, orchestration, infrastructure as code, monitoring, and incident response


Ensure tasks reflect practical engineering constraints rather than purely theoretical exercises


Define clear expected outcomes and validation criteria


Maintain technical realism across infrastructure and platform-engineering workflows


Reference Solutions & Reproducibility




Write working reference solutions for DevOps and infrastructure tasks


Provide clear setup, execution, and validation steps


Build reproducible solutions that can be verified consistently


Document assumptions, dependencies, and environment requirements


Maintain a strict quality bar for technical correctness


AI Output Review & Technical Evaluation




Review AI-generated solutions to DevOps and infrastructure problems


Identify technical failures, incorrect assumptions, and incomplete implementations


Write precise corrections explaining both the issue and the appropriate solution


Evaluate outputs for correctness, reliability, and operational viability


Provide structured feedback that improves future task and evaluation quality


Cloud, Containers & Infrastructure as Code




Work with Docker, Kubernetes, and modern containerised infrastructure


Design or evaluate CI/CD workflows using platforms such as GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, or Jenkins


Apply Infrastructure as Code using Terraform, Ansible, Pulumi, CloudFormation, or comparable tools


Work across at least one major cloud platform such as AWS, GCP, or Azure


Apply strong Linux and Git practices across technical workflows


Platform Reliability & Engineering Quality




Assess infrastructure solutions for scalability, reliability, maintainability, and security


Diagnose deployment, configuration, or automation failures


Incorporate observability and operational best practices where relevant


Maintain consistent standards across production-style engineering tasks


Contribute structured feedback that supports continuous improvement of technical evaluation frameworks


Ideal Profile




3+ years of professional experience in DevOps, SRE, Platform Engineering, Infrastructure Engineering, or a closely related role


Strong coding ability in Python, Go, Bash, TypeScript, or comparable languages


Ability to work with real application and infrastructure code rather than relying solely on basic scripting


Practical experience with CI/CD systems such as GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, or Jenkins


Strong experience with Docker and Kubernetes


Hands-on experience with at least one major cloud platform, including AWS, GCP, or Azure


Infrastructure as Code experience with Terraform, Ansible, Pulumi, CloudFormation, or comparable tooling


Advanced Linux and Git proficiency


Strong written and spoken English


Experience with observability platforms such as Prometheus, Grafana, Datadog, or OpenTelemetry is advantageous


Security, secrets-management, or platform-reliability experience is beneficial


Open-source contributions or technical-writing experience are valued


Previous AI-training or model-evaluation experience is beneficial but not required


No prior experience in AI is required


Engagement Details




Independent contractor engagement


Fully remote


Compensation: $50–$100/hour


Minimum availability: approximately 20 hours per week


Work will involve DevOps task design, reference-solution development, AI-output evaluation, cloud infrastructure, CI/CD, containers, and Infrastructure as Code


Strong coding ability and hands-on infrastructure experience are central to this engagement


Assignments may involve Kubernetes, Terraform, Linux, Git, Docker, cloud platforms, monitoring, and incident-response scenarios


Project scope, workload, technical focus, and evaluation standards may evolve depending on project requirements


Work must be completed without using confidential or proprietary information belonging to any employer, client, institution, or other third party


About the Platform


This opportunity is available through 24-MAG LLC. We connect experienced professionals with remote consulting opportunities across technical, evaluation, and project-based workstreams.


By submitting this application, you acknowledge that your information may be processed by 24-MAG LLC for recruitment and opportunity matching in accordance with our Privacy Policy: https://www.24-mag.com/privacy-policy﻿',
