    'Georgia Tek Systems', NULL, 'GTRI DevOps Engineer - Atlanta GA (100% remote)', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Title/Role: GTRI DevOps Engineer
 Worksite Address: Atlanta GA
 Work Arrangement: Remote
 Agency Interview Type: Either Web Cam or In Person
 Start Date: 06/24/2024 - End Date: 12/31/2024

This position is 100% remote. Out-of-state candidates are accepted. East Coast strongly preferred

The selected candidate must be a U.S. Citizen

Complete Description:

Department: Enterprise Systems Department

Job Overview:
The Georgia Tech Research Institute (GTRI) Enterprise Systems Department department is seeking a highly skilled and motivated DevOps Engineer to join our dynamic team of innovators in driving advancements in implementing and managing CI/CD pipelines for software development teams. The ideal candidate will have a deep understanding of DevOps best practices and experience with GitLab, AWS, Azure, Kubernetes, Docker, and other related technologies. This individual will play a key role in modernizing our software development processes and infrastructure to achieve greater automation, scalability, and efficiency. 

Responsibilities and Duties:Collaborate with software development teams to understand current processes and identify areas for CI/CD implementation and improvement.Design, implement, and maintain CI/CD pipelines for multiple software projects.Automate deployment processes to ensure smooth and efficient delivery of software updates.Monitor and optimize infrastructure performance and scalability.Work with development teams to troubleshoot build and deployment issues.Stay updated on industry best practices and technology advancements to continuously improve our CI/CD capabilities.
Qualifications:Bachelor''s degree in Computer Science or related fieldProven experience in a DevOps or Cloud Engineer roleStrong understanding of GitLab, AWS, Azure, Kubernetes, Docker, and other relevant tools and technologiesExperience with infrastructure as code tools such as Terraform or CloudFormationProficiency in scripting and automation using tools like Bash, Python, or PowerShellExcellent problem-solving, communication, and collaboration skills to effectively work with cross-functional teams, researchers, and faculty.Relevant certifications (e.g., AWS Certified DevOps Engineer, Azure DevOps Engineer Expert) a plus.5 years of relevant working experience.
Remote

Skills:
Amazon Web Services (AWS), Automation, Bash Scripting, Best Practices, Cloud Computing, Computer Science, Continuous Deployment/Delivery, Continuous Improvement, Continuous Integration, Cross-Functional, DevOps, Docker, Identify Issues, Microsoft Windows Azure, Multitasking, Performance Tuning/Optimization, Problem Solving Skills, Python Programming/Scripting Language, Scripting (Scripting Languages), Software Administration, Software Development, Software Engineering, Team Player, Technical Research, United States Citizen, Webcams, Windows PowerShell


