INSERT INTO jobs (
    company_name, company_logo_url, position_title, location, employment_type,
    salary_min, salary_max, salary_currency, salary_period, description,
    status, posted_at, external_id, source, url, is_remote, tags
) VALUES (
    'Scan.com', 'https://serpapi.com/searches/6ab375a3c2034812ac7582c5/images/iDkOsfKEdgWmu8VAR8O2ZtJLb0hsZVf7vwr4yHefib4.jpeg', 'Senior DevOps Engineer', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'We''re Scan.com. We''re building America''s national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging. Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.

We manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end. Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway. Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.

We''re looking for a Senior DevOps Engineer at an exciting time. We''ve raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.

Millions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.

What You Will Be Getting Involved In

Scan.com''s infrastructure is the layer on which everything else depends. Our marketplace, integrations, data warehouse, and clinical workflows all run on a cloud environment that must be reliable, observable, secure, and compliant with the frameworks governing healthcare technology. As we scale, that layer needs to scale with us, and the engineering practices around it need to mature at the same pace.

We are seeking a Senior DevOps Engineer to join our Infrastructure team as we expand the DevOps function. This is a hands-on senior role that combines deep technical execution with the kind of engineering judgment that shapes how a growing infrastructure team operates. You will report into our Infrastructure leadership and work closely with Engineering, Security, and Compliance across a HIPAA-regulated environment.

Role

As a scale-up business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:



Provide hands-on DevOps work across the network, servers, and cloud platforms, operating as a senior technical contributor from day oneEnsure DevOps and Engineering processes align with security best practices, and help embed those practices deeper into how the broader engineering org worksImplement monitoring, logging, and observability solutions using CloudWatch, DataDog, and other tooling to ensure system health and performance are visible and actionableAutomate security scanning, vulnerability assessments, and compliance checks within CI/CD pipelines, closing the gap between "we run scans" and "we act on what they find"Ensure all infrastructure is managed via IaC (Terraform), so that reproducibility and version control are properties of the system rather than aspirationsArchitect and implement deployment strategies, including blue-green deployments, canary releases, and automated rollbacks, with the goal of making production changes safe by defaultAdvance software supply chain security across dependency risk, artifact integrity, and code signing, and guide implementation patterns that other engineering teams can adoptLeverage AI-powered tools to analyze risks, identify consolidation opportunities across our estate, and generate assessment summaries that would otherwise require significant manual effort

THE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR ARE

Deep infrastructure command. In your first 90 days, we would expect you to build a comprehensive understanding of our cloud environment: the services we run, how they are configured, where the risk concentrations are, and where the highest-leverage improvements sit. You are the person the team looks to for confident answers about how our infrastructure actually works.IaC coverage and reliability. By the end of your first year, our Terraform footprint has meaningfully expanded, drift has been reduced, and the infrastructure that matters most is managed in code without exceptions. New environments and services are provisioned reproducibly rather than by hand.A stronger security and compliance posture. You have materially contributed to how we implement HIPAA, SOC 2, and ISO controls in our cloud environment. Compliance is not a periodic scramble but a set of automated checks and repeatable patterns that hold up under audit and under real-world pressure.Deployment maturity. Blue-green deployments, canary releases, and automated rollbacks are in production for the services where they matter most. The team''s default expectation for a production change is that it can be made safely and reverted quickly.An AI-native infrastructure team. You have raised the bar for how the Infrastructure function uses AI, both in your own work and in your coaching of the team. Configuration, scripting, troubleshooting, and risk analysis are all being accelerated by AI in ways that are measurable, safe, and repeatable.

What You Might Bring To The Table

You don''t need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it''s your first role or your fifth, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:

Six or more years of experience in DevOps, Infrastructure, and Cloud Engineering, with a track record of operating at a senior technical level in production environmentsDeep understanding of HIPAA, SOC-2, and ISO compliance frameworks and their technical implementation. You have translated compliance requirements into infrastructure controlsExpertise in AWS, including EKS, RDS, Security Hub, Identity Center, and Control Tower. You are fluent in the AWS security and account management primitives, not just the compute and storage onesStrong working knowledge of Postgres or other relational databases, including operational responsibilities such as performance tuning, backups, and failoverStrong expertise in CI/CD pipelines, particularly GitHub Actions & ArgoCD, and a clear point of view on how to structure pipelines that are fast, safe, and observableSolid grasp of security best practices in CI/CD pipelines and cloud infrastructure, with the practical experience to know where the common failure modes areHands-on experience with containerization (Docker, Kubernetes) and Infrastructure as Code (Terraform), including building and managing declarative GitOps deployment patterns via ArgoCD to handle application lifecycle management at scaleGenuine AI fluency in your daily infrastructure practice. You use AI tools daily to accelerate IaC, scripting, and troubleshooting. Rather than relying on AI as an occasional aid, you understand how to structure configurations so AI agents can reliably consume them, and you actively evaluate the security and quality of AI-generated code. Candidates who treat AI as a novelty rather than a core part of how they work will not be competitive for this roleAdvanced knowledge of Cloudflare and its role in edge, security, and performance architecturesExcellent problem-solving skills and the ability to troubleshoot complex deployment issues under production pressure without losing composure or accuracy

Ai Requirements

At Scan.com, AI isn''t a side project; it''s how we work. We expect everyone to use AI to think faster, remove drudgery, and multiply their output. What we care about is judgment: knowing when AI makes you sharper, when it doesn''t, and how to use it responsibly around patient data. We''ll assess this in the way that matters for this role, using the tier below. You don''t need to be an engineer. You need to be someone who reaches for the best tool and gets more done as a result.

Tier 1 — For this role, the expectation is that you are an AI-Native. You build with AI directly, shipping, automating, or prototyping real work with LLMs and agents, and have clear judgment on where humans must stay in the loop. (this is typically aligned to engineering, data, product, ops automation, RevOps)You build with AI, not just alongside it. You''ve shipped, automated, or prototyped something real using LLMs, agents, or AI tooling.You can explain a workflow you redesigned so that a machine does the boring 80%.You have a view on where agentic systems help and where a human must stay in the loop, especially in regulated, PHI-adjacent work.Assessment: a practical exercise where you use AI tools live or in a take-home.
A VIEW ON OUR CULTURE

We''re building something that matters. Every scan we speed up is a real person waiting on an answer, and that urgency runs through everything we do. We move fast, we own outcomes, and take pride in our output. If you like ambiguity, working with ambitious people, and want your work to visibly move the needle, you''ll feel at home here. To be successful at Scan.com, you must embody our values.

OUR VALUES

Always Play Offense

If we''re not growing, we''re dying. Everyone needs a bias for action. Speed and momentum, combined with quality execution, propel our business forward.

You don''t quit on hard problems. Fail fast, dust off, go again.You celebrate wins, then seek the next opportunity.You see it, you fix it. No task is beneath you, at any level.

Build with the Best

The company we build is the team we build. If we don''t have the right people in the right seats, doing the right things, we will fail.

Talent recognizes talent. You actively bring quality hires into the business.You trust your colleagues to deliver.You open-source your knowledge. You''re never a single point of failure.

Care Deeply, Challenge Directly

Care enough to have the hard conversations, and don''t dwell on them. Don''t go up the chain to communicate. Go straight to the person.

Strong opinions, weakly held. You welcome challenge and feedback.You get to the point: direct challenge plus an alternative solution.You ask "why". Before calling something bad, understand why it exists.

Embrace Growth, Be Curious

Push the limits of your understanding and potential and you will be supported to get better.

You proactively seek feedback, whatever your level.You invest in understanding our business: teams, customers, processes.You invest in your own growth and are willing to unlearn.

We''re a high-performing team with low ego. We hire people who are brilliant and kind, who give it straight, back it up with evidence, and change their mind when the facts change. We''ll give you real ownership early, the tools to do your best work, and colleagues who raise your game. In return, we ask for high standards, genuine care for patients and each other, and the drive to leave things better than you found them. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!

How We Will Interview You

We keep our interview process short and sweet, and we''re a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:

Introductory call/interview with our Senior Talent Partner. The call is via telephone and will last around 30 minutes.Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a video call with the hiring manager for around 45 minutes. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.''Scan Standard'' interview, where our panel screens for values alignment and the success factors that matter at Scan.com. You will also be assessed on your AI fluency at the stage and depth relevant to your role (see AI Requirements above).Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, length varies depending on how many people and whether in person or via video call.Offer!

What We Offer

We go beyond the basics with our benefits package. We believe great work starts with supporting our people. Here''s what you can expect from us:

Salary range of $165,000 - $185,000Flexible remote or hybrid work optionsDedicated personal development budgetMedical, vision, and dental coverage28+ days of paid time off across PTO and wellbeing days, so you can show up at your bestPaid parental leave401k retirement planAll the equipment you need to do your best workInclusive, people-first policies designed by our team, for our team

DIVERSITY AT SCAN.COM

Scan.com is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.

We are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.

Our ambition is for our team to be representative of society''s diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.

If you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at people@scan.com.

We look forward to receiving your application!',
    'active', '2026-09-02T06:51:23.442360+00:00', '', 'google_jobs', 'https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/senior-devops-engineer-at-scan-com-4448632411', TRUE, ARRAY['Devops Engineer','Remote']::TEXT[]
)
