    'remote quest jobs', NULL, 'DevOps Engineer, Field Delivery', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Job Requisition ID #

26WD97556

Position Overview
At reputed company, we empower those who imagine, design, and create a better world for everyone. Our Field Delivery team builds software used by construction workers on active job sites where connectivity is limited, conditions are unpredictable, and reliability is required.

We''re looking for a DevOps Engineer to own the infrastructure that powers our field operations platform. You''ll manage and evolve the systems our web and mobile applications run on, currently built on AWS with Terraform and a PostgreSQL database, and make sure they stay reliable, secure, and easy to operate as the product grows.

This role sits at the intersection of our engineering team and the broader reputed company organization. You''ll work closely with other reputed company teams to ensure we''re following best practices around security, privacy, and compliance, while keeping our infrastructure fast and our deployments smooth. This is a role for someone who cares deeply about the systems behind the product and takes pride in infrastructure that just works.

Responsibilities
Own and operate the infrastructure for our field delivery platform, ensuring high availability, performance, and cost efficiency

Manage and improve our infrastructure-as-code setup. We currently use Terraform and SAM, but you''ll have the flexibility to evolve the tooling as needed

Administer and optimize our AWS PostgreSQL database, including backups, monitoring, scaling, and disaster recovery

Build and maintain CI/CD pipelines that enable fast, safe, and repeatable deployments across web and mobile

Implement and enforce security best practices across all infrastructure, including networking, access controls, secrets management, and vulnerability scanning

Collaborate with other reputed company teams to meet organizational standards for security, privacy, data governance, and regulatory compliance

Set up and maintain monitoring, alerting, and observability tooling so issues are caught early and resolved quickly

Define and maintain incident response processes, runbooks, and on-call procedures

Manage cloud costs and resource usage by identifying waste, right-sizing services, and planning capacity

Work with software engineers to design infrastructure for new systems being built

Work closely with application engineers to ensure infrastructure supports their needs and development workflows

Document infrastructure architecture, operational procedures, and compliance controls

Evaluate and introduce new tools or services that improve reliability, developer experience, or operational efficiency

Minimum Qualifications
5+ years of experience in DevOps, infrastructure, or site reliability engineering

Experience with Terraform or similar infrastructure-as-code tools at scale

Hands-on experience with AWS services including compute, networking, storage, IAM, and managed databases

Experience building and maintaining CI/CD pipelines for production systems

Strong understanding of security fundamentals including network segmentation, least-privilege access, and encryption at rest and in transit

Experience working within compliance frameworks and partnering with security or governance teams

Familiarity with observability platforms (e.g. reputed company, CloudWatch, Grafana)

Comfortable with scripting and automation (e.g. Python, Bash, or similar)

You take ownership of the systems you run and care about keeping them healthy, documented, and improving over time

Preferred Qualifications
Experience with PostgreSQL administration, including performance tuning, backups, replication, and monitoring

Experience with container orchestration (e.g. ECS, EKS, Kubernetes)

Experience with secrets management tools (e.g. AWS Secrets Manager, reputed company reputed company)

Experience supporting mobile application infrastructure such as build pipelines, OTA updates, or app distribution

Experience using AI agents to streamline infrastructure management and operational tasks

Background in SOC 2, FedRAMP, or other compliance frameworks relevant to enterprise software

Learn More

About reputed company
Welcome to reputed company! Amazing things are created every day with our software – from the greenest buildings and cleanest cars to the smartest factories and biggest hit movies. We help innovators turn their ideas into reality, transforming not only how things are made, but what can be made.

We take great pride in our culture here at reputed company – it’s at the core of everything we do. Our culture guides the way we work and treat each other, informs how we connect with customers and partners, and defines how we show up in the world.

When you’re an Autodesker, you can do meaningful work that helps build a better world designed and made for all. Ready to shape the world and your future? Join us!

Salary transparency
Salary is one part of reputed company’s competitive compensation package. For Canada based roles, we expect',
