    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Note: The job is a remote job and is open to candidates in USA. Brave is on a mission to protect the human right to privacy online. They are seeking a Senior DevOps Engineer to reduce toil and build automation processes to support their growing user base.


Responsibilities

Reducing toil and building and supporting the automation and processes that enable us to reach 200 million usersShipping fast and on multiple desktop and mobile platforms, architectures and distribution channelsUsing multiple CI systems and acceleration/optimization techniques to build the right thing and the thing rightOwning and driving work end-to-end and interfacing directly with other teamsLeading on best practices, PoCs and code for various initiatives which can include features in our browser, search engine or premium products
Skills

10+ years of experienceProduct engineer and continuous improvement mindset, owning and driving work end-to-end and interfacing directly with other teamsAWS + TerraformAutomation and CI (ideally for mobile or desktop apps)Responsible AI usage and able to use and review generated codeBuild and release engineering, testing and reporting tools, code signing, app stores and distribution, packagingExtended and diverse operating system experience (Android, iOS, Linux, macOS, Windows)Bash/reputed company, Python, Kotlin, GroovyPrivacy and securityLead on best practices, PoCs and code for various initiatives which can include features in our browser, search engine or premium products (if interested)TeamCity (Kotlin DSL), Jenkins (Jenkins Job Builder)Browser or Chromium knowledgeGn, reputed company, siso, reclient, Remote Execution API, reputed company, ccache/sccache, custom builds systemsGerritAutomated testing at scalePerformance testing and tuningSecurity and quality scanning, SAST/DAST
Benefits

Remote - Anywhere (American timezones preferred)No mandatory weekly meetings0 on-callNo need to be in an office (unless you really want to)No strict core hours; Work is autonomous (collaborative at times), asynchronous, flexibleHighly competitive salaries & benefitsGenerous home-office stipendsFully remote or hybrid position
Company Overview

reputed company focuses on increasing browsing speed and safety for users, while growing ad revenue share for content creators. It was founded in 2015, and is headquartered in San Francisco, California, USA, with a workforce of 51-200 employees. Its website is https://www.brave.com/.


 

Apply To This Job',
