IaC coverage and reliability. By the end of your first year, our Terraform footprint has meaningfully expanded, drift has been reduced, and the infrastructure that matters most is managed in code without exceptions. New environments and services are provisioned reproducibly rather than by hand.
A stronger security and compliance posture. You have materially contributed to how we implement HIPAA, SOC 2, and ISO controls in our cloud environment. Compliance is not a periodic scramble but a set of automated checks and repeatable patterns that hold up under audit and under real-world pressure.
Deployment maturity. Blue-green deployments, canary releases, and automated rollbacks are in production for the services where they matter most. The team''s default expectation for a production change is that it can be made safely and reverted quickly.
An AI-native infrastructure team. You have raised the bar for how the Infrastructure function uses AI, both in your own work and in your coaching of the team. Configuration, scripting, troubleshooting, and risk analysis are all being accelerated by AI in ways that are measurable, safe, and repeatable.
WHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLEYou don''t need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it''s your first role or your fifth, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:
Six or more years of experience in DevOps, Infrastructure, and Cloud Engineering, with a track record of operating at a senior technical level in production environments
Deep understanding of HIPAA, SOC-2, and ISO compliance frameworks and their technical implementation. You have translated compliance requirements into infrastructure controls
Expertise in AWS, including EKS, RDS, Security Hub, Identity Center, and Control Tower. You are fluent in the AWS security and account management primitives, not just the compute and storage ones
Strong working knowledge of Postgres or other relational databases, including operational responsibilities such as performance tuning, backups, and failover
Strong expertise in CI/CD pipelines, particularly GitHub Actions & ArgoCD, and a clear point of view on how to structure pipelines that are fast, safe, and observable
Solid grasp of security best practices in CI/CD pipelines and cloud infrastructure, with the practical experience to know where the common failure modes are
Hands-on experience with containerization (Docker, Kubernetes) and Infrastructure as Code (Terraform), including building and managing declarative GitOps deployment patterns via ArgoCD to handle application lifecycle management at scale
Genuine AI fluency in your daily infrastructure practice. You use AI tools daily to accelerate IaC, scripting, and troubleshooting. Rather than relying on AI as an occasional aid, you understand how to structure configurations so AI agents can reliably consume them, and you actively evaluate the security and quality of AI-generated code. Candidates who treat AI as a novelty rather than a core part of how they work will not be competitive for this role
Advanced knowledge of Cloudflare and its role in edge, security, and performance architectures
Excellent problem-solving skills and the ability to troubleshoot complex deployment issues under production pressure without losing composure or accuracy
HOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOUWe keep our interview process short and sweet, and we''re a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order depending on team availability:
Introductory call with our Senior Talent Partner, approximately 30 minutes by phone.
Video call with the hiring manager, approximately 45 minutes, a structured deep-dive into the role and technical domain.
Assessment stage, which may be a take-home exercise, in-person session, or additional video calls. We''re mindful of your time.
Meet the founders and/or other team members.
Offer!
BENEFITSWe go beyond the basics with our benefits package. Here''s what you can expect from us:
Competitive salary range, plus performance bonus and equity
401k
Healthcare, Vision, and Dental
All equipment needed to do your role effectively
Flexible and remote/hybrid working options
Personal development budgets
18 days PTO plus public holidays
10 paid sick days
Inclusive policies designed by our team, for our team
DIVERSITY AT SCAN.COMScan.com is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.
We are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.
Our ambition is for our team to be representative of the diversity in society, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.


If you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at people@scan.com.


We look forward to receiving your application!',
    'active', '2026-08-27T06:51:23.443025+00:00', '', 'google_jobs', 'https://bebee.com/us/jobs/senior-devops-engineer-scancom--fj-2293007825', TRUE, ARRAY['Devops Engineer','Remote']::TEXT[]
)
