    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'A boutique software consulting firm is seeking a fully remote Azure DevOps Engineer to join a growing team focused on delivering cloud-first solutions for enterprise clients. This full-time opportunity centers around designing, automating, and managing Azure infrastructure using modern Infrastructure as Code practices, with a strong emphasis on Azure, Bicep, Azure DevOps, CI/CD automation, and Kubernetes technologies. The organization specializes in customizing and integrating complex software platforms, and this role will be instrumental in provisioning and supporting the cloud environments that power those solutions.
 
 If you''re passionate about automation and enjoy building cloud environments the right way from day one, this is an opportunity to make a significant impact. The ideal candidate is someone who thrives in consulting environments, enjoys solving unique infrastructure challenges, and can help drive best practices across cloud architecture, deployment automation, and platform engineering. You''ll work with a variety of Azure services, contribute to scalable client deployments, and have the opportunity to influence cloud strategy while remaining highly hands-on with modern DevOps tooling.
 
 Required Skills & Experience 

 4+ years of experience as an Azure DevOps Engineer, Cloud Engineer, or Platform Engineer Strong experience building and managing Azure infrastructure in enterprise environments Advanced experience developing Infrastructure as Code solutions using Bicep Expertise creating and maintaining Azure DevOps CI/CD pipelines Experience provisioning and managing Azure networking, security, and identity services Hands-on experience with Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) Strong PowerShell scripting and automation experience Experience implementing monitoring, alerting, and operational best practices Knowledge of Git-based source control workflows Experience troubleshooting complex cloud infrastructure issues Strong communication skills and ability to work directly with technical stakeholders  Desired Skills & Experience  Azure certifications (AZ-104, AZ-305, AZ-400, or similar) Experience working within consulting or client-facing environments Knowledge of Terraform and other Infrastructure as Code platforms Experience with container technologies and Kubernetes administration Familiarity with Azure Landing Zones and governance frameworks Experience implementing cloud security controls and compliance standards Knowledge of SQL, application integrations, and middleware technologies Exposure to Azure Monitor, Log Analytics, and Application Insights Experience supporting highly available and disaster recovery-focused environments  What You Will Be Doing
 Tech Breakdown  40% Azure Infrastructure & Platform Services 25% Bicep / Infrastructure as Code 20% Azure DevOps Pipelines & CI/CD 15% AKS, PowerShell, Monitoring & Automation  Daily Responsibilities  80% Hands On 5% Management Duties 15% Team Collaboration  The Offer  Bonus eligible  You will receive the following benefits:  Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Vacation Time 401(k) Fully Remote Work Environment  Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the US on a full-time basis now and in the future.',
