    'BDR Solutions LLC', 'https://serpapi.com/searches/6ab375b9b4ab7229b4ac8819/images/GRW0io5VBJQf_pvmnwEx6Yo3v_F40rMC_KKp3FDPnwc.png', 'Cloud Engineer - Mid-Level', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    110000, 170000, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Description




About us:




BDR Solutions, LLC, (BDR) supports the U.S. Federal Government in successfully achieving its mission and goals. Our service and solution delivery starts with understanding each client''s end-state, and then seamlessly integrating within each Agency''s organization to improve and enhance business and technical operations and deployments.




(Military Veterans are highly encouraged to apply)




Role Overview:




BDR Solutions LLC is seeking a Cloud Engineer to support mission-critical federal platforms. This role focuses on AWS infrastructure, Kubernetes (EKS), and DevSecOps-driven operations to ensure high availability, scalability, and security.




Key responsibilities include managing cloud environments, maintaining CI/CD pipelines, optimizing performance and costs, and supporting 24x7 operations. The ideal candidate brings deep AWS expertise, strong automation skills, and experience working in secure, high-availability environments.




Responsibilities:





 Active MBI - mandatory; candidates in process do NOT qualify
 Current or recent IRS contract experience strongly preferred
 7+ years of hands-on AWS cloud engineering
 Expert-level Terraform for automated IaC provisioning and management
 DevSecOps CI/CD pipeline design using GitHub Actions with SAST/DAST/secrets scanning
 Experience with Databricks Asset Bundles for workspace deployment automation
 Strong proficiency with EKS, Lambda, S3, IAM, and VPC networking
 Experience with blue/green and canary deployment strategies
 AWS DevOps Engineer Professional or AWS Certified Developer preferred
 Willingness to support 24x7 on-call including off-hours deployment windows
 Bachelor''s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or related field



Required Minimum Qualifications:





 Design and implement the foundational DevSecOps CI/CD pipeline architecture using GitHub Actions for tenant onboarding automation
 Automate tenant workspace provisioning and IaC-based onboarding workflows using Terraform and Databricks Asset Bundles
 Enforce code quality, dependency scanning, and policy-as-code with approval gates and full audit trails
 Implement secure environment promotion through dev/test/prod for deliverables
 Support 24x7 CI/CD pipeline monitoring and failure remediation
 Maintain Platform Operations Runbook and IaC Baselines
 Contribute to tenant satisfaction by ensuring provisioning pipelines meet the 10-business-day SLA
 Clearance Required: Minimum Background Investigation (MBI) - ACTIVE



Tools and Platforms:





 Experience with Infrastructure as Code tools (Terraform, CloudFormation, ARM/Bicep)
 Familiarity with CI/CD tools (Jenkins, GitHub Actions, Azure DevOps)
 Experience with Docker and Kubernetes
 Solid understanding of networking fundamentals (TCP/IP, DNS, VPNs)



Clearance Required: Minimum Background Investigation (MBI) - ACTIVE




Nice to Have Qualifications:





 Cloud certifications (AWS, Azure, or GCP)
 Experience with monitoring tools (CloudWatch, Prometheus, Grafana)
 Knowledge of microservices architecture
 Experience with automated testing and deployment strategies





In addition, U.S Citizenship is required. Select applicants will be subject to a government security investigation and must meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information and be able to obtain a government-granted security clearance. Individuals may also be subject to a background investigation including, but not limited to criminal history, employment and education verification, drug testing, and creditworthiness.




This position is contingent upon contract award. Employment is not guaranteed and will proceed only if the associated contract is awarded and funded.




The compensation range for this position is $110,000 - 170,000. Compensation decisions depend on a wide range of factors, including but not limited to location, skill sets, experience and training, security clearances, licensure and certifications, and other business and organizational needs.',
    'active', '2026-09-18T06:51:23.444169+00:00', '', 'google_jobs', 'https://www.ziprecruiter.com/c/BDR-Solutions/Job/Cloud-Engineer-Mid-Level/-in-Herndon,VA?jid=879ca08241507621', TRUE, ARRAY['Cloud Engineer','Remote']::TEXT[]
)
