    136000, 204000, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'About the position

As a Principal Engineer, Cloud, you will play a pivotal role in shaping CarMax’s next-generation cloud infrastructure. This is your opportunity to join an innovative team that is redefining the automotive retail experience through cutting-edge technology. You’ll lead efforts to design, build, and evolve scalable cloud platforms, ensuring reliability, security, and resilience for our customer-facing applications. By leveraging your expertise in cloud engineering and automation, you’ll help CarMax deliver a seamless, best-in-class experience that empowers customers to buy the vehicles they want—on their terms.

Responsibilities

Develop and implement self-service capabilities and automation tools to accelerate delivery and improve operational efficiency.Collaborate with cross-functional teams in design, product management, and architecture to transform innovative ideas into practical solutions.Provide technical leadership and guidance, fostering a culture of continuous improvement and agile practices.Consult with internal stakeholders to evolve cloud platforms and optimize performance using modern engineering principles.Stay ahead of industry trends, applying best practices to enhance reliability, scalability, and security across cloud environments.Requirements

Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science or related field, or equivalent experience with 7+ years in technology roles.4+ years of hands-on experience building cloud infrastructure (Azure preferred; AWS or Google Cloud considered).3+ years of scripting or coding experience in languages such as Python, PowerShell, or similar.Expertise in cloud networking, storage, virtualization, and access control, including hybrid environments.Proven ability to design and deploy resilient cloud architectures and manage CI/CD pipelines using tools like Azure DevOps or TeamCity.Strong leadership skills with experience mentoring teams and driving cross-functional initiatives.Passion for automation and eliminating manual processes to improve efficiency and scalability.Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Sponsorship will not be considered for this specific role.Benefits

Paid sick timeVacation timeHoliday timeFloating holidayHoliday Premium PayPaid time away with no specified limit as needed for sick, vacation, bereavement, jury duty, holidays, floating holiday, etc. subject to manager approval.',
