    'The Intersect Group', NULL, 'Lead Data Engineer - Retail Media Network', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Lead Data Engineer – Retail Media Network (Snowflake)


Job Order: 250473
Employment Type: Contract-to-hire
Location: Remote (United States)
 

Overview


Help power a fast-growing Retail Media Network by building the data foundation that fuels smarter advertising and customer insights. As a Lead Data Engineer, you’ll design and optimize analytics-focused data architectures in Snowflake, enabling reliable, high-performance datasets for BI and data science teams across retail advertising and customer data ecosystems. You’ll own key technical decisions, drive best practices, and lead the evolution of scalable pipelines and models that support both batch and real-time (or near real-time) use cases.
 

Required Skills



6+ years of data engineering experience, including lead-level ownership of delivery and architecture decisionsStrong, hands-on expertise with Snowflake (required), including:
	Snowpipe, Streams, TasksAdvanced SQL and data transformation expertisePython (preferred, especially for Snowpark)Proven experience building analytics-focused data warehousesStrong understanding of:
	Dimensional modeling (Star Schema, Snowflake Schema; facts & dimensions)Data warehousing architectureData quality and governance practicesEntity relationships and schema designOLTP vs. OLAP concepts and analytical data lifecycleMedallion architecture concepts

Nice to Have Skills

Experience with integration/orchestration tools such as dbt, Airflow, and FivetranBackground in Retail or Retail Media Network environmentsFamiliarity with:
	Customer data platforms (CDPs)Advertising / attribution datasetsExperience supporting analytics and BI use cases at scaleExposure to AI/ML data pipelines and building AI-ready datasets

Preferred Education and Experience

Preferred experience: 6+ years in data engineering with demonstrated ownership of end-to-end warehouse/pipeline architecture and delivery in analytics-heavy environmentsEducation: Not specified in the provided job details

Work Authorization


Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States.
 

Additional Details

Travel: Not specified in the provided job detailsCertifications: Not specified in the provided job details
How to apply: Not specified in the provided job details.

Remote

Skills:
Advertising, Analysis Skills, Artificial Intelligence (AI), Best Practices, Business Intelligence, Customer/Client Research, Data Management, Data Quality, Data Science, Data Sets, Data Warehousing, Database Design, Dimensional Modeling, Ecosystems, Engineering, OLAP (OnLine Analytical Processing), Python Programming/Scripting Language, Retail, SQL (Structured Query Language), Snowflake Schema, Star Schema, Training Data Sets, Transaction Processing/Management, Use Cases


