    'TEKsystems', 'https://serpapi.com/searches/6ab376771de06477ef4ec2bd/images/faQozd8xv3t1HKibSDZucdMtFn8LKFq6OthHjgIUtNc.jpeg', '[Hiring] Identity and Access Management Specialist @TEKsystems', 'Remote', 'Contractor',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Role Description




 Our client is searching for an InfoSec and Compliance Specialist for a remote temp-to-perm role.




 ***All candidates must work directly for TEKsystems on a W2 basis until this position converts to full-time employment and no sponsorship is available now or in the future***




 
  
   Identity Federation:
  
  Architect enterprise SSO using Keycloak, SAML 2.0, and OpenID Connect (OIDC). Configure Entra ID (Azure AD) and Google Cloud Identity as identity brokers.
 
 
  
   Access Governance:
  
  Establish centralized RBAC, multi-factor authentication (MFA), and zero-trust policies across all platform boundaries.
 
 
  
   Supply Chain Security:
  
  Manage GitHub Advanced Security (GHAS), enforcing Dependabot alerts, secret scanning, static analysis (CodeQL/SAST), and branch protection rules.
 
 
  
   Cloud Security:
  
  Implement portable secrets management and monitor service-to-service security (e.g., mTLS) across K8s cluster boundaries.
 
 
  
   Audit & Compliance:
  
  Lead audit readiness, vulnerability scanning, and compliance enforcement for frameworks like SOC 2 or ISO 27001.
 


 This position is for a senior-level Engineer. Pay will be based on experience and a drug background check is required.






 Benefits




 
  Medical, dental & vision
 
 
  Critical Illness, Accident, and Hospital
 
 
  401(k) Retirement Plan – Pre-tax and Roth post-tax contributions available
 
 
  Life Insurance (Voluntary Life & AD&D for the employee and dependents)
 
 
  Short and long-term disability
 
 
  Health Spending Account (HSA)
 
 
  Transportation benefits
 
 
  Employee Assistance Program
 
 
  Time Off/Leave (PTO, Vacation or Sick Leave)
 


 Company Description




 This is a Contract to Hire position based out of Houston, TX.




 The pay range for this position is $50.00 - $65.00/hr. Individual compensation offered for this position within this range will depend on many factors, including qualifications, skills, relevant experience, job knowledge, geographic location, internal equity, and other pertinent job-related factors.




 Eligibility requirements apply to some benefits and may depend on your job classification and length of employment. Benefits are subject to change and may be subject to specific elections, plan, or program terms. If eligible, the benefits available for this temporary role may include the following:




 This is a fully remote position.




 This position is anticipated to close on Oct 4, 2026.',
