    'Tidal Vision', 'https://serpapi.com/searches/6ab3767c3d06ea115d66a04a/images/nQtMdcObXuLAP4k-jhKlTe515B49PjJKqnc0ru1awxI.jpeg', 'Stormwater Sampler, Sample Pick-up Courier', 'Remote', 'Part-time',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Job Description:

 Complete assigned sample pick-up routes throughout San Diego County, ranging from a few stops to approximately 20 client locations per day Use a personal vehicle for required travel between locations Pick up replenishment sampling kits and completed stormwater samples from assigned client locations Verify sample labels, physical Chain of Custody documentation, packaging, and separation of samples from different facilities Provide replacement sampling kits to clients and address missing documentation when possible Communicate delays, wait times, scheduling issues, route concerns, and supply needs to Frog Environmental Deliver samples and required documentation to Frog Environmental the same day and obtain receipt confirmation Coordinate after-hours deliveries when necessary Monitor weather forecasts and deploy for authorized stormwater sampling assignments Collect stormwater samples according to permit requirements, company procedures, regulatory timeframes, and established protocols Wear PPE and follow safety and clean-sampling procedures Photograph sampling locations and discharge points and submit same-day documentation Perform field pH testing and complete Chain of Custody and Sample Event Observation forms Label, ice, refrigerate, deliver, or ship samples as required Refer client questions to appropriate Frog Environmental staff Record work time, mileage, and expenses according to company proceduresRequirements:

 Valid driver''s license, reliable personal vehicle, and automobile insurance required Ability and willingness to travel throughout Los Angeles, Orange, and Riverside Counties Reliable, punctual, and able to work independently while managing assigned routes and sampling activities Strong attention to detail and organizational skills, including accurate handling of samples and documentation Ability to follow sampling, safety, chain-of-custody, and other established procedures Strong professional communication skills Ability to use a personal cell phone for work-related communication, documentation, and navigation Ability to complete required training Background check required Ability to safely handle and transport sample containers, coolers, sampling kits, and related supplies Ability to wear required personal protective equipment (PPE) Ability to work at client facilities, including outdoor work in rain and varying weather conditionsBenefits:

 Eligible benefits in accordance with applicable plan terms and eligibility requirements $50.00 per hour for approximately two hours of required initial sampling training $200 sampling incentive for successfully sampling 1–2 assigned client facilities during a deployment $50 for each additional client facility successfully sampled during the same deployment $5 for each eligible scheduled sample pick-up stop completed in accordance with program requirements Mileage reimbursement in accordance with the applicable California mileage reimbursement rate Cell phone reimbursement in accordance with Company policy and applicable California law Overtime paid in accordance with applicable California law At least two hours of pay per deployment, or any greater amount required by applicable California law',
    'active', '2026-09-18T06:51:23.446209+00:00', '', 'google_jobs', 'https://www.remoterocketship.com/us/company/tidalvision/jobs/stormwater-sampler-sample-pick-up-courier-california-remote/', TRUE, ARRAY['Data Scientist','Remote']::TEXT[]
)
