    160000, 220000, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Job Description:

 Drive Prompt’s mission to improve healthcare through modern technology including AI Lead AI projects from ideation → architecture → production → iteration until features are widely adopted and loved! Develop and deploy real-time AI systems involving speech and natural language understanding (e.g., transcription, summarization, classification) Build robust model and prompt pipelines for LLM-powered workflows with high accuracy and monitoring standards Partner with Product and Engineering to identify high-leverage AI opportunities and deliver measurable outcomes Help develop Prompt’s strategic AI roadmap across speech, NLP, and core automation workflows Apply AI to improve client and internal operations including clinical documentation, customer support, and billing workflows Develop a deep understanding of Prompt’s product, customers, and the business of rehab therapy Help grow and lead the AI team, including training and development of junior team membersRequirements:

 4+ years of experience building AI/ML systems in industry or academia, with meaningful production ownership Strong experience building and evaluating NLP and/or LLM systems (e.g., retrieval, summarization, classification, extraction, agent workflows) Experience working with speech-related pipelines in production or near-real-time settings (e.g., speech-to-text, spoken intent classification, conversational AI) Track record of benchmarking and iteratively improving accuracy, cost, and latency Enthusiastic and pragmatic problem-solving mindset Excellent communication skills, with the ability to explain complex AI concepts to non-technical stakeholders Python (>3.9) Docker (Basics) AWS familiarity (S3, RDS, EC2) preferred Willingness to learn and deeply understand the healthcare sector, specifically physical therapy, occupational therapy, and speech therapy Please only apply if you are interested in a heavy code contribution role; this is not an engineering management position, though growth opportunities exist over timeBenefits:

 Competitive salaries Remote/hybrid environment Potential equity compensation for outstanding performance Flexible PTO Company-wide sponsored lunches Company paid disability and life insurance benefits Company paid family and medical leave Medical, dental, and vision insurance benefits Discounted pet insurance FSA/DCA and commuter benefits 401k Credits for online fitness classes/gym memberships Recovery suite at HQ – includes a cold plunge, sauna, and shower',
