INSERT INTO jobs (
    company_name, company_logo_url, position_title, location, employment_type,
    salary_min, salary_max, salary_currency, salary_period, description,
    status, posted_at, external_id, source, url, is_remote, tags
) VALUES (
    'SmartAdvocate', NULL, 'Senior AI Engineer – Neural Networks, Voice & Autonomous Agents', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'About SmartAdvocate & SmartIntelligence


SmartAdvocate is a leading legal case management software engineered to streamline operations, litigation workflows, and client management for law firms. Through our proprietary AI initiative, SmartIntelligence, we are building next-generation artificial intelligence tools directly into our platform.


We are expanding our engineering team to develop state-of-the-art voice agents for automated intake and autonomous background agents for complex legal document processing, search, and workflow automation.


Position overview


We are seeking a Senior AI Engineer specializing in Neural Networks, Voice, and Autonomous Background Agents to join our team. In this role, you will move beyond standard API integrations to design, fine-tune, and deploy proprietary deep learning models tailored to legal and medical domain requirements.


You will lead the development of ultra-low latency voice agents capable of managing complex phone intakes while accurately handling specialized legal and medical terminology. Additionally, you will build and optimize fine-tuned Small Language Models (SLMs) and custom vector retrieval architectures to power autonomous background agents across the SmartAdvocate platform.


Key Responsibilities


Voice Agent & Speech Architecture



 Fine-tune and optimize Speech-to-Text (STT) and Text-to-Speech (TTS) neural models on domain-specific datasets such as legal terminology, medical ICD codes, and mass tort nomenclature.
 Engineer end-to-end streaming audio pipelines using WebRTC, voice activity detection (VAD), and low-latency audio processing to enable natural, real-time conversational flows.
 Reduce voice response latency to sub-second levels for automated client intake and phone workflows.

Background Agents & Small Language Models (SLMs)



 Train, fine-tune, and quantize open-weight models such as Llama, Mistral, and Qwen for local and private cloud deployments to minimize operational inference costs.
 Build multi-step autonomous background agents for automated case file classification, medical record summarization, and task routing.
 Implement robust agent monitoring, logit analysis, and debugging frameworks to diagnose attention drift and prevent hallucinations in automated workflows.

Information Retrieval & Neural Search



 Design custom dense retrieval models and neural re-rankers optimized for long-form court filings, legal briefs, and client records.
 Enhance Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipelines within SmartIntelligence to ensure high precision and zero-hallucination data extraction.

Qualifications & Requirements


Technical Core



 Deep Learning Expertise: Strong foundation in deep neural network architectures, attention mechanisms, Transformer models, and gradient optimization strategies.
 Framework Proficiency: Hands-on mastery of PyTorch, Hugging Face Transformers, ONNX Runtime, TensorRT, and vLLM or similar high-throughput inference engines.
 Voice & Audio AI: Proven experience with speech recognition models such as Whisper or Wav2Vec2, streaming TTS architectures, and raw audio tensor manipulation.
 Agentic Workflows & RAG: Track record of deploying production-grade agent architectures, custom vector search spaces, and specialized embedding models.
 Engineering Stack: Advanced knowledge of Python, asynchronous programming via asyncio, gRPC/REST APIs, Docker, and GPU-accelerated cloud infrastructure across AWS, Azure, or GCP.

Legal AI Background (Highly Preferred)



 Legal AI Industry & Law Firm Experience: Prior experience developing artificial intelligence applications directly within a law firm environment, or at a legal technology entity that builds AI software actively utilized by law firms, is highly preferred.
 Domain Adaptation: Proven success adapting deep learning architectures, LLMs, and speech models to handle legal workflows, statutory logic, complex court filings, or medical-legal documentation.

What We Offer



 The opportunity to shape core intellectual property in the legal technology industry.
 Direct involvement in scaling SmartIntelligence across hundreds of law firms nationwide.
 Collaborative engineering environment focused on privacy, proprietary capability, and technical excellence.

How we hire


We read work, not keywords. Our process is deliberately short:



 Resume and portfolio review
 A 45-minute conversation about systems you have built and operated
 A short technical exercise against a realistic problem from our actual domain — not a whiteboard puzzle
 A final conversation with our CTO and the AI team

Additional Information/Benefits:


A dynamic, rapidly growing company, focused on helping organizations thrive. We offer a competitive compensation and benefits package including medical insurance, PTO and 401K Plan. We are an equal opportunity employer. We maintain a safe and healthy working environment.


Pay: From $200,000.00 per year


Benefits:



 401(k)
 401(k) matching
 Dental insurance
 Flexible spending account
 Health insurance
 Health savings account
 Life insurance
 Paid time off
 Parental leave
 Vision insurance

Experience:



 Legal Software: 1 year (Required)

Work Location: Remote',
    'active', '2026-09-18T06:51:23.448840+00:00', '', 'google_jobs', 'https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=7228b6287063e20f', TRUE, ARRAY['Ai Engineer','Remote']::TEXT[]
