    'Cognizant Technology Solutions', 'https://serpapi.com/searches/6ab376b413f4b6f5ea1ef040/images/enoGhQ3N-pItuwB_3vDtOW9-7TM8auOOmw4_asluyFc.jpeg', 'Senior Android Developer (Kotlin/Java) - Open for remote', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    68000, 110000, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'About the role




As a Senior Android Developer, you will make an impact by designing, developing, testing, and deploying high-quality Android applications using Kotlin and Java. You will be a valued member of the application development team and work collaboratively with Technical Program Managers, technical leads, developers, and other stakeholders to translate business requirements into reliable mobile solutions.



Work model




This is a remote role based on business requirements in Bentonville, AR. Regardless of work arrangement, we support a healthy work-life balance through our wellbeing programs.




The working arrangements for this role are accurate as of the date of posting. This may change based on the project you''re engaged in, as well as business and client requirements. Rest assured; we will always be clear about role expectations.



Important Disclaimer:



Please note: A few of our roles may require in-person interviews at Cognizant offices or client locations, depending on project or client needs.



In this role, you will:



 Design and develop scalable, maintainable, and high-performing Android applications using Kotlin and Java.
 Analyze business requirements, recommend technical solutions, and lead discussions with Technical Program Managers, technical leads, and project stakeholders.
 Build application features in accordance with established coding standards and Android development best practices.
 Create unit tests and meet or exceed the code-coverage targets established by the project.
 Support application testing, release management, and successful deployment to production.
 Implement appropriate application monitoring solutions based on client and project requirements.
 Prepare and maintain technical designs, service specifications, and application documentation.
 Provide technical guidance to developers preparing functional and technical specifications.


What you need to have to be considered



 Six or more years of professional Android application development experience.
 Strong hands-on experience with the Android SDK and Android Studio.
 Proficiency in Kotlin and Java for Android application development.
 Experience designing and developing applications using MVVM, MVC, or MVI architecture.
 Experience building unit tests and working toward established code-coverage requirements.
 Knowledge of Android application testing, production deployment, and app distribution processes.
 Ability to analyze business requirements and translate them into effective technical solutions.
 Strong communication skills with the ability to lead technical conversations and collaborate with cross-functional stakeholders.


These will help you stand out



 Experience providing technical guidance or mentorship to Android developers.
 Knowledge of application monitoring and production-support practices.
 Experience preparing technical designs, service specifications, and functional documentation.
 Familiarity with cloud platforms such as Microsoft Azure or Google Cloud Platform.
 Experience contributing to coding standards, design reviews, and application-quality initiatives.



We''re excited to meet people who share our mission and can make an impact in a variety of ways. Don''t hesitate to apply, even if you only meet the minimum requirements listed. Think about your transferable experiences and unique skills that make you stand out as someone who can bring new and exciting things to this role.



Salary and Other Compensation: 




Applications will be accepted until October 3rd, 2026.




The annual salary for this position is between $68,000 - $110,000 depending on experience and other qualifications of the successful candidate. 




This position is also eligible for Cognizant''s discretionary annual incentive program, based on performance and subject to the terms of Cognizant''s applicable plans. 



Benefits: Cognizant offers the following benefits for this position, subject to applicable eligibility requirements:




• Medical/Dental/Vision/Life Insurance




• Paid holidays plus Paid Time Off




• 401(k) plan and contributions




• Long-term/Short-term Disability




• Paid Parental Leave




• Employee Stock Purchase Plan



Disclaimer:




The salary, other compensation, and benefits information is accurate as of the date of this posting. Cognizant reserves the right to modify this information at any time, subject to applicable law.




The working arrangements for this role are accurate as of the date of posting. This may change based on the project you''re engaged in, as well as business and client requirements. Rest assured; we will always be clear about role expectations.




Applicants may be required to attend interviews in person or by video conference. In addition, candidates may be required to present their current state or government issued ID during each interview.



About Cognizant: 


Cognizant (Nasdaq: CTSH) is an AI Builder and technology services provider, bridging the gap between AI investment and enterprise value by building full-stack AI solutions for our clients. Our deep industry, process and engineering expertise enables us to build an organization''s unique context into technology systems that amplify human potential, drive tangible outcomes and keep global enterprises ahead in a fast-changing world. See how at cognizant.ai or @cognizant.



Additional employment information


Compensation information is accurate as of the date of this posting. Cognizant reserves the right to modify this information at any time, subject to applicable law.




Applicants may be required to attend interviews in person or by video conference. In addition, candidates may be required to present their current state or government issued ID during each interview.




Cognizant is an equal opportunity employer. Your application and candidacy will not be considered based on race, color, sex, religion, creed, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, veteran status or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws.




If you have a disability that requires reasonable accommodation to search for a job opening or submit an application, please email [email protected] for roles based in the Americas or [email protected] for roles based in India.',
    'active', '2026-09-18T06:51:23.449310+00:00', '', 'google_jobs', 'https://www.ziprecruiter.com/c/cognizant/Job/Senior-Android-Developer-(Kotlin-Java)-Open-for-remote/-in-Bentonville,AR?jid=02b9dc346e5cdc5e', TRUE, ARRAY['Android Developer','Remote']::TEXT[]
)
