    'remote quest jobs', NULL, 'Experienced Android Developer for Cricket App', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'We are looking for an experienced Android developer to build a professional Cricket Live Score Android application from scratch.

The app should have a clean, modern UI and be designed with scalability in mind so additional leagues and tournaments can be added easily in the future.

The project includes Android app development, backend development, admin panel, database, API integration, and deployment support.

Scope of Work

1. Live Score Integration

Integrate a Cricket Live Score API with support for:

Live Scores

Live Match Updates

Upcoming Matches

Completed Matches

Full Scorecard

Ball-by-ball Commentary (if available)

Match Info

Playing XI

Match Odds (if API supports)

Pitch Report

Venue Information

Toss Details

Match Results

Series & Tournaments

2. Manual Live Score Update

Sometimes third-party APIs delay score updates.

Need an admin feature that allows manual updates for selected matches.

Admin should be able to update:

Runs

Wickets

Overs

Current Batsmen

Current Bowler

Innings Status

Toss

Match Result

Commentary

Match Notes

Match Status

Manual updates should immediately override API data whenever required.

3. News Module

Need a complete news publishing system.

Features:

Create News

Edit News

Delete News

Featured Image

Categories

Rich Text Editor

Push Notification on Publish

The app should automatically display published news.

4. Admin Panel

Need a complete web-based admin panel.

Features:

Secure Login

Dashboard

Match Management

Manual Score Updates

News Management

Push Notifications

Advertisement Control

API Configuration

User Statistics

Match Visibility Controls

5. Website Backend & API Optimization (Very Important)

This project must not reputed company live score data directly from the cricket API inside the Android app.

Instead, use the following architecture:

Cricket Live Score API

│

▼

Website Backend (Cache + Database)

│

▼

Android App

Requirements

Server fetches data from the Cricket API.

Store live data in the website database.

Android app fetches data only from our own backend.

Implement intelligent caching to reduce API usage.

Refresh intervals should be configurable (e.g., every 30–60 seconds depending on the match state).

Thousands of users should be able to use the app without increasing third-party API requests.

This requirement is essential to minimize API costs and improve scalability.

6. Advertisement Integration

Integrate reputed company AdMob.

Support:

Banner Ads

Native Ads

Interstitial Ads

App Open Ads

Rewarded Ads (Optional)

Ads should be easy to enable, disable, or update.

7. Push Notifications

Firebase Cloud Messaging integration.

Notifications for:

Match Starting

Toss Result

reputed company

Four

Six

Fifty

Century

Innings Break

Match Finished

Breaking News

8. Additional Features

Match Search

Favorite Teams

Share Match

Pull to Refresh

Offline Cache

Fast Loading

Material Design UI

reputed company Screen

App Update Dialog

Privacy Policy

Contact Page

About Page

Settings

Dark Mode

Deliverables

Developer must provide:

Complete Android Source Code

Complete Backend Source Code

Admin Panel Source Code

Database Structure

API Documentation

Installation & Deployment Guide

Assistance with Play Store release

Bug fixes after delivery

Preferred Tech Stack

Android

Kotlin (preferred) or Java

MVVM Architecture

Retrofit

Room Database

Backend

Laravel (preferred) or Node.js

MySQL

Admin Panel

Laravel Blade or React

Notifications

Firebase Cloud Messaging

Important Technical Requirement

The solution should be built for high scalability and low API costs.

The backend should cache live score data and expose its own API to the Android application, ensuring that API requests remain low even with a large number of concurrent users.

Ideal Candidate

We''re looking for someone who:

Has built cricket or sports applications before.

Has experience with real-time APIs.

Has Android and backend development expertise.

Understands API optimization and caching.

Can write clean, maintainable code.

Provides post-launch support.

When Applying, Please Include

Links to similar Android apps you''ve developed.

Experience working with cricket or sports APIs.

Your recommended tech stack.

Estimated development timeline.

Fixed-price quote.

Support period after project completion.

Suggestions to improve scalability, performance, and reduce third-party API usage.

Apply tot his job

Apply To this Job',
    'active', '2026-09-17T06:51:23.449808+00:00', '', 'google_jobs', 'https://us.remotejobs.dedyn.io/job/3438707', TRUE, ARRAY['Android Developer','Remote']::TEXT[]
)
