) VALUES (
    'Halvik', 'https://serpapi.com/searches/6ab376c6f0114a6ac76713f7/images/aHBgjiWka7MqBhsdW6w8XxWJmvxmfpFgPgLWqhDJITo.jpeg', 'Scrum Master/Data QA Engineer', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    110000, 125000, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Halvik Corp delivers a wide range of services to 13 executive agencies and 15 independent agencies. Halvik is a highly successful WOB business with more than 50 prime contracts and 500+ professionals delivering Digital Services, Advanced Analytics, Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning, Cyber Security and Cutting-Edge Technology across the US Government. Be a part of something special!


  Position Overview


 Halvik is seeking a Scrum Master / Data QA Tester to support the U.S. Department of Transportation (DOT) IPNDS modernization effort. This role combines Agile/Kanban delivery facilitation with hands-on quality assurance for enterprise data pipelines and analytics products. The position will work closely with the Product Owner, Business Analyst, data engineers, technical leads, architects, and DevSecOps/CloudOps teams to maintain delivery flow, remove blockers, execute data-focused testing, manage defects, and support controlled releases across Dev, Test, and Production environments.


  Core Responsibilities


 
   Strategic Execution: Facilitate Agile/Kanban delivery ceremonies and working sessions, including daily flow reviews, backlog replenishment, refinement, planning, delivery reviews, retrospectives, and blocker follow-up. Maintain Jira boards, workflow status, WIP visibility, dependencies, delivery metrics, and action items.
   Operational Oversight: Develop and execute test plans, test cases, regression suites, and release-readiness checks for data pipelines, data products, and analytics solutions. Track testing progress, defects, retesting, and exit criteria through completion.
   Collaboration: Partner with the Product Owner and Business Analyst to understand acceptance criteria and expected outcomes, and coordinate with data engineers, architects, BI developers, security, and DevSecOps/CloudOps teams to resolve blockers, defects, and release dependencies. The separate Business Analyst role will retain primary ownership of business requirements and detailed functional analysis.
   Technical Performance: Perform data-focused QA using SQL and analytical tools, including source-to-target reconciliation, record-count and field-level validation, business-rule checks, duplicate/null detection, incremental-load validation, rerun/recovery testing, and verification of downstream reports and datasets. Validate Bronze/Silver/Gold processing and data quality controls where applicable.
   DefectRelease Management: Log, prioritize, and track defects; maintain traceable test evidence; coordinate UAT support and release checklists; validate deployment prerequisites and approvals; and perform post-deployment smoke/regression testing in coordination with Data Engineering and DevSecOps/CloudOps teams.
 
  Minimum Requirements


 
   Education: Bachelor''s degree in Information Systems, Computer Science, Business, Data Analytics, Engineering, or a related field; equivalent relevant experience may be considered.
   Experience: Minimum of 5 years of combined experience in Scrum Master/Agile delivery, software or data quality assurance, testing, or related roles supporting enterprise data, analytics, or application systems.
   Technical Proficiency: Working-to-intermediate SQL skills for data validation and troubleshooting; hands-on experience with Jira or similar Agile tools; experience testing ETL/ELT, data warehouse/lakehouse, APIs, or analytics solutions; familiarity with defect management, regression testing, UAT support, and release validation.
   Compliance: Must meet applicable U.S. DOT contract security and suitability requirements and follow established change management, data protection, access control, testing, documentation, and release governance processes.
   Certifications: Certified ScrumMaster (CSM), Professional Scrum Master (PSM), SAFe, Kanban, ISTQB, or comparable Agile/testing certification preferred; equivalent demonstrated experience will be considered.
 
 


 Preferred Expertise


 
  Demonstrated success supporting U.S. DOT/BTS, FAA, or other Federal data/technology programs; experience with aviation, transportation, or other high-volume regulated data is a plus.
  Experience testing Databricks/Delta Lake or similar data platforms, including source-to-target reconciliation, data quality controls, batch/incremental pipelines, SQL validation, regression testing, and production-release support.
  Familiarity with CI/CD and controlled Dev-Test-Prod promotion, Git-based workflows, test automation using Python or comparable tools, and collaboration with DevSecOps/CloudOps teams. Strong facilitation, communication, analytical, and problem-solving skills.
 
 
 Halvik offers a competitive full benefits package including:Company-supported medical, dental, vision, life, STD, and LTD insuranceBenefits include 11 federal holidays and PTOEligible employees may receive performance-based incentives in recognition of individual and/or team achievements.401(k) with company matchingFlexible Spending Accounts for commuter, medical, and dependent care expensesTuition AssistanceCharitable Contribution matching 
 
Halvik Corp is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or veteran status.',
