    'Blu Omega', 'https://serpapi.com/searches/6ab376c7f607a9eab7a299ea/images/XxGMEib-v38V4O-uP84HnYth6PPJ6UGdquwP0s1Kud8.png', 'QA Engineer and Tester', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'QA Engineer and Tester







Remote













Blu Omega is seeking a QA Engineer and Tester to support a federal health program focused on enterprise data, analytics, and application modernization. This role operates within a remote environment and is responsible for ensuring mission-critical applications and data platforms are stable, secure, and fully validated before deployment. The position requires experience supporting quality assurance, automation, and cloud-based testing within a mission-driven environment.













Program Overview













Blu Omega supports mission-focused organizations across the federal healthcare sector, delivering innovative solutions to modernize applications and improve software quality.













Key Details







Location: Remote







Clearance: Ability to obtain and maintain a Public Trust or Suitability/Fitness determination







Salary Range:







Salary Minimum: $0.00







Salary Maximum: $115,000.00













Responsibilities


Design, develop, and maintain automated testing frameworks for web applications, APIs, and data platforms
Build scalable cloud-based test environments using AWS, Azure, Docker, or similar technologies
Apply AI-enabled testing techniques, such as GitHub Copilot and agentic UI automation, to accelerate validation efforts
Perform automated and manual testing, including functional, regression, usability, user acceptance testing, and API validation
Develop and execute comprehensive test plans, test scripts, and validation strategies for enterprise applications and data platforms
Implement and support CI/CD pipelines using Azure DevOps, GitHub Actions, Bitbucket, Jenkins, or similar tools
Integrate automated testing into CI/CD workflows to enable continuous validation and release quality improvement
Collaborate with developers, business analysts, Product Owners, and QA team members to identify defects and optimize testing coverage
Analyze testing results, identify quality risks, and recommend improvements
Maintain detailed documentation of test cases, defect reports, test results, and quality metrics
Mentor junior QA team members and promote automation best practices
Ensure applications meet functional, security, performance, and accessibility standards
Required Qualifications
4+ years of experience designing, developing, and maintaining automated testing frameworks
4+ years of programming or scripting experience using Python, Java, Groovy, SQL, or Bash
2+ years supporting CI/CD pipelines with Azure DevOps, GitHub Actions, Bitbucket, Jenkins, or similar
Hands-on experience developing and executing automated API tests
Experience building scalable test environments using cloud technologies such as AWS, Azure, or Docker
Experience applying AI-powered QA tools such as GitHub Copilot or agentic UI automation
Strong understanding of test methodologies, quality engineering practices, and SDLC
Excellent troubleshooting, analytical, and problem-solving skills
Experience working in Agile environments with cross-functional teams
Effective written and verbal communication skills
Ability to obtain and maintain a Public Trust or Suitability/Fitness determination
Bachelor’s degree in computer science, engineering, information technology, or a related field
Preferred Qualifications
Experience testing data pipelines, data platforms, or solutions built within Palantir Foundry
Experience with MuleSoft, API platforms, enterprise integrations, or middleware technologies
Knowledge of human-centered design, usability testing, and Section 508 compliance
Experience supporting federal government or healthcare environments
Mentoring junior QA professionals and contributing to quality standards
Compensation


Salary Range:


Final compensation is based on technical skills, experience, education, certifications, and compliance.




Blu Omega Benefits & Perks
Medical, Dental, and Vision coverage through national providers
401(k) with company match (eligible after 6 months; vesting applies)
Company-paid Life and AD&D insurance with additional voluntary options
Short-term disability (company-paid) and long-term disability options
Employee Assistance Program (EAP) with 24/7 confidential support and mental health resources
Telehealth and virtual care options available through medical plans
Pet insurance, legal services, and identity theft protection options
Paid Time Off (PTO) for eligible employees
Paid federal holidays for salaried employees
Access to wellness programs, discounts, and lifestyle benefits
Benefits eligibility and offerings may vary based on role, employment status, and program requirements.
Company Overview


Blu Omega is a Woman-Owned Small Business (WOSB) delivering technology and cybersecurity solutions to federal agencies and enterprise clients nationwide. Headquartered in Ashburn, VA, we support mission-critical programs across civilian and defense sectors, including health, national security, and regulatory environments.




We partner with government agencies and large integrators to provide expertise in cybersecurity operations, cloud and infrastructure modernization, data and analytics, and enterprise IT support. Our teams are experienced operating within federal contracting environments, supporting task orders, recompetes, and programs requiring cleared personnel and compliant delivery.




Equal Opportunity Employer


All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability.




