) VALUES (
    'Dexcom', 'https://serpapi.com/images/i/iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAADgAAAA4CAMAAACfWMssAAAAY1BMVEX___8AowBWtkj0-vPM58kAoQBqvV-a0JRLszvc7tomqQARpQC94Lme0pfk8eLI5MTt9ut3wm7D4r-Axndvv2T5-_ii1J223LGo1aKTzYyu2alBrzCJyYIuqhWNyoY5rSZiulefpAgpAAAAvElEQVRIie3Qyw6DIBCF4cNFHcULCKiVKn3_p6ymmya163Yx344JfzIZgDHG2H-pnXMjoDwFG8sBqtSYSM7oA3mFpXJ08-Q_Q23WsWghJW6EvYFPWEStajT3c1iZehG6LfqLcMTmYPbeZ2BPMp7_z7lGJ1TXYBbQ4jrMAeZRDcdrbQJe4fAWxuuwtcWKFBAVVqPKx7GehY2mQ5lQfQ8T0XTcSCbSMc2weYDPqYOmJHtMGe0W9fYZMsYY-60nOcYJ3FHHaPIAAAAASUVORK5CYII.png', 'Product Manager, Consumer Mobile App', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Meet the team: 

Join our dynamic and innovative consumer team at the crux of innovation, technology, and consumer products! We are dedicated to empowering individuals to take control of their metabolic health through cutting-edge biosensor technology and intuitive app experiences. If you''re passionate about pushing the boundaries of what''s possible and thrive in fast-moving environments, we want you on our team.

As Product Manager for the Stelo app, you’ll lead the development of in-app features that help users monitor, understand, and improve their metabolic health. You’ll work cross-functionally with design, engineering, clinical, and marketing teams to deliver experiences that are evidence-based, engaging, and impactful.

Where you come in: 

  * Continuously discover and prioritize opportunities that will drive our product and business outcomes
  * Translate user needs, clinical insights, and business goals into clear product requirements
  * Collaborate with UX/UI designers to craft intuitive and motivating user experiences
  * Partner with engineering to prioritize and deliver high-quality mobile features
  * Monitor product performance, user feedback, and health outcomes to iterate and improve
  * Contribute to the product strategy and roadmap for the Stelo app, and take ownership of driving execution from concept to launch.
  * Stay current on trends in metabolic health, digital therapeutics, and mobile health innovation



What makes you successful: 

  * 3+ years of product management experience for a mobile app, ideally in digital health or wellness
  * Strong understanding of, and passion for metabolic health
  * Proven success building and launching mobile apps (iOS/Android)
  * Experience with wearable tech, CGM, and/or health data platforms
  * Familiarity with regulatory considerations in consumer health apps
  * Experience working with cross-functional teams in agile environments
  * Excellent communication, prioritization, and stakeholder management skills
  * Passion for empowering people to live healthier lives through technology



What you’ll get: 

  * A front row seat to life changing CGM technology. Learn about our brave #dexcomwarriors community.
  * A full and comprehensive benefits program.
  * Growth opportunities on a global scale.
  * Access to career development through in-house learning programs and/or qualified tuition reimbursement.
  * An exciting and innovative, industry-leading organization committed to our employees, customers, and the communities we serve.



Travel Required: 

  * 5-15%



Experience and Education Requirements:

  * Typically requires a Bachelor’s degree and a minimum of 8-12 years of related experience.
  * At this level a graduate degree may be desirable with 4 years of related experience.



Remote Workplace: Your location will be a home office; you are not required to live within commuting distance of your assigned Dexcom site (typically 75 miles/120km). If you reside within commuting distance of a Dexcom site (typically 75 miles/120km) a hybrid working environment may be available. Ask about our Flex workplace option.

  


Please note: The information contained herein is not intended to be an all-inclusive list of the duties and responsibilities of the job, nor are they intended to be an all-inclusive list of the skills and abilities required to do the job. Management may, at its discretion, assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. The duties and responsibilities in this job description may be subject to change at any time due to reasonable accommodation or other reasons. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. 

  


An Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, national origin, or protected veteran status and will not be discriminated against on the basis of disability. Dexcom’s AAP may be viewed upon request by contacting Talent Acquisition at talentacquisition@dexcom.com. 

  


If you are an individual with a disability and would like to request a reasonable accommodation as part of the employment selection process, please contact Dexcom Talent Acquisition at talentacquisition@dexcom.com. 

  


Meritain, an Aetna Company, creates and publishes the Machine-Readable Files on behalf of Dexcom. To link to the Machine-Readable Files, please click on the URL provided: https://health1.meritain.com/app/public/#/one/insurerCode=MERITAIN_I&brandCode=MERITAINOVER/machine-readable-transparency-in-coverage?reportingEntityType=TPA_19874&lock=true

  


AI in Hiring Notice: We may use AI supported tools to help make our hiring process more efficient, consistent, and accessible for candidates around the world. All hiring decisions are made by people.

  


Salary:

$122,500.00 - $204,100.00',
    'active', '2026-09-17T06:51:23.451727+00:00', '', 'google_jobs', 'https://careers.dexcom.com/careers/job/44540163', TRUE, ARRAY['Product Manager','Remote']::TEXT[]
)
