    'Globalchannelmanagement', NULL, 'Remote Senior Product Manager – Next-Gen Cloud Infrastructure & GPU Platforms', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Senior Product Manager – Next-Gen Cloud Infrastructure & GPU Platforms

We are seeking a highly technical Senior Product Manager to lead the strategy and roadmap for our next-generation cloud infrastructure, compute, and GPU platforms. This role is ideal for a product leader who can bridge the gap between complex technology, customer needs, and business strategy.

You will work closely with engineering, architecture, sales, customers, and technology partners to develop scalable infrastructure products supporting AI, HPC, enterprise, and cloud workloads.

To land this role, you must have an elite track record of managing hyperscale or cutting-edge infrastructure. We are specifically looking for candidates who meet the following high-bar criteria:

Professional Experience:12+ years of experience in technical product management, cloud architecture, or infrastructure engineering.Target Background: A proven track record at premier infrastructure organizations such as hyperscalers (AWS, Azure, GCP, OCI), alternative clouds (DigitalOcean, Linode, Vultr, Equinix, Cloudflare), or enterprise infrastructure software leaders (VMware, Nutanix, Red Hat, OpenStack).AI & Accelerated Computing:Deep technical knowledge of GPU architectures, CUDA, AI/HPC workloads, cluster scaling, and accelerated computing.Core Systems & Virtualization: Robust understanding of CPU/server architecture, Linux, networking, storage, containers, multi-tenant environments, and hypervisors (KVM, VMware, Hyper-V, Xen).Modern Developer Ecosystem:Familiarity with Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tools like Terraform, Pulumi, Ansible, or CloudFormation to build developer-first APIs and automated experiences.Cloud Economics:Advanced financial acumen with hands-on experience driving pricing strategies, capacity utilization, margin maximization, and TCO analyses.Technical Leadership:Exceptional communication and alignment skills, with a demonstrated ability to influence highly technical engineering teams and collaborate with executive leadership.Education: Bachelor''s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or equivalent practical deeply technical experience.What You''ll Do

Strategy & Vision:Define the product vision, strategy, roadmap, and priorities for cloud compute and GPU platforms.Technical Product Management:Translate customer and market needs into product requirements and technical specifications. Partner with engineering on CPU/GPU, server, networking, storage, and virtualization technologies.Lifecycle Management:Manage products throughout their lifecycle, from concept and launch through optimization and end-of-life.Cloud Economics:Develop business cases, pricing strategies, financial models, and TCO/profitability analyses.Go-To-Market: Develop go-to-market strategies with sales, marketing, and solutions engineering. Collaborate with technology partners on integrations and infrastructure roadmaps.Developer Experience:Define APIs, automation, and developer experiences that make infrastructure easier to consume.Metrics & Alignment:Track key metrics including utilization, adoption, revenue, performance, and profitability. Build alignment across engineering, executive leadership, and customer-facing teams.
Remote

Skills:
Amazon Web Services (AWS), Analysis Skills, Ansible, Application Programming Interface (API), Artificial Intelligence (AI), Automation, Business Case, Business Strategy, CPU (Central Processing Unit), CUDA (Compute Unified Device Architecture), Capacity Utilization, Cloud Architecture, Cloud Computing, Computer Science, Customer Relations, Economics, Ecosystems, Financial Modeling, GCP (Good Clinical Practices), GPU (Graphics Processing Unit), Hypervisors, Infrastructure Software, K Virtual Machine (KVM), Leadership, Linux Operating System, Market Entry Strategy, Marketing Software, Metrics, Microsoft Hyper-V, Microsoft Windows Azure, Product Lifecycle Management, Product Management, Product Pricing, Product Strategy, Product Support, Profit & Loss, Profit & Loss Analysis, Red Hat Linux Operating System, Sales, Sales Strategy, Scalable System Development, Server Architecture, Software Engineering, Technical Leadership, Total Cost of Ownership, VMWare, Virtualization, Xen Hypervisor


