INSERT INTO jobs (
    company_name, company_logo_url, position_title, location, employment_type,
    salary_min, salary_max, salary_currency, salary_period, description,
    status, posted_at, external_id, source, url, is_remote, tags
) VALUES (
    'Euronet Worldwide, Inc.', NULL, 'Senior Product Manager-Card Issuing Platform', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Euronet facilitates the movement of payments around the world, serving as a critical link between financial institutions, retailers, service providers, and their end consumers. Following Euronet''s acquisition of CoreCard, we are expanding our issuer processing and card issuing platform capabilities. This position is focused exclusively on card issuing platform products and requires direct issuer processing product management experience. 

We are seeking a Senior Product Manager who can bridge business and technology to ensure existing platform offerings and new product features result in exceptional experience for our clients.  This is a highly visible position within a flexible and start-up style business unit with a unique market position. High visibility with leadership and direct impact on platform evolution.

This role requires deep, hands-on experience building and managing card issuing platform products and issuer processing solutions for credit and/or debit cards. 

Responsibilities: 

Establish product direction and tactical roadmaps for the products, including product line extensions, target markets supported and GTM plans to deliver world-class products and features which level-set the competitive landscape. Engage in market research, customer and competitive analysis, and market needs analysis for credit issuing products, and prioritize the roadmap based on fast-changing market conditions.   Work closely with Product Delivery and Development to ensure requirements are interpreted correctly in detailed design specifications and in the construction of the product assigned. Develop and manage multiple product programs simultaneously utilizing local and global team members, drive collaboration across functional areas, and ensure results meet key performance and business objectives.Collaborate across the organization and externally to identify opportunities for integration, new products and revenue growth. Assistance/Coordination with product marketing management related to product objectives, development of presentations and sales decks, development and maintenance of product brochures and website/PR content.  Respond to product inquiries, deliver product demonstrations, manage RFI/RFP responses, pricing analysis, and contract negotiation.Assist in the creation and publication of the Product User Guides, Service Catalogs, roadmaps, and other product related communication.  Act as the product conduit for compliance requirements and ensure all mandates and compliance changes are being included in the roadmap and release plans. BA/BS qualification in a technology or business field.7+ years of product management experience with card issuing platforms and issuer processing (credit/debit)Demonstrated experience owning product strategy, roadmaps, and feature delivery for issuer processing platformsStrong understanding of card lifecycle management, authorization, and issuer processing technologiesStrong communication skills, both oral and written, to concisely communicate key issues/results in a manner appropriate to the audience, including the executive level.Ability to work independently, with limited direction.Entrepreneurial attitude with leadership skills to leverage matrix organizations.Ability to build relationships with and influence other functional areas as well as external entities.Euronet employees enjoy outstanding benefits, including:

401(k) PlanHealth/Dental/Vision InsuranceEmployee Stock Purchase PlanCompany-paid Life InsuranceCompany-paid disability insuranceTuition ReimbursementPaid Time OffPaid Volunteer DaysPaid HolidaysCasual Office AttirePlus many more employee perks & incentives!We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, age, disability status, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.
All application materials including that which is submitted on our applicant tracking system, including resumes, cover letters, and responses, must accurately reflect your own qualifications and experience. The use of any false or misleading content - including any information that is created through the use of AI that is not a true and accurate description of your skills, qualifications, or experience - is strictly prohibited. By submitting your application, you certify that all information provided is truthful and created by you. Any violation may result in disqualification from the recruitment process. If your employment has already begun and it is later discovered that you misrepresented your skills or qualifications, whether through false information or AI‑generated content, this may result in disciplinary action toward you, including but not limited to the termination of your employment.',
