INSERT INTO jobs (
    company_name, company_logo_url, position_title, location, employment_type,
    salary_min, salary_max, salary_currency, salary_period, description,
    status, posted_at, external_id, source, url, is_remote, tags
) VALUES (
    'Openly', 'https://serpapi.com/searches/6ab376d9b24c5d42c30cc8e3/images/FAWUSlZ_zzIYJuMcD-i7iYOg8KSt1hxCkeI16bycl7Y.jpeg', 'Regional Insurance Product Manager (Remote, US)', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    115680, 137370, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Ready for your next chapter?Openly has redefined the insurance experience—replacing decades of complexity with clarity. We’re the insurance provider for people who expect more and the partner independent agents have been waiting for.

Building a better future for personal lines insurance requires diverse expertise and thoughtful execution. We bring together dedicated problem-solvers who are excited to challenge the status quo and do meaningful work.

What Sets Us ApartTechnology That Delivers:We leverage cutting-edge data to modernize underwriting and deliver tailored insurance solutions.

Superior Protection:Highly customizable coverage designed to match the unique needs of modern homeowners.

A Seamless Experience:Frictionless workflows for independent agents and fast, human-centered care for policyholders.

Our Core ValuesAt Openly, our people are just as important as our product. Collaboration, communication, and work-life balance aren''t just nice-to-haves—they are core to who we are. We believe a great company is built on a foundation of shared values, which is why we seek out individuals driven by integrity, empathy, teamwork, curiosity, and a healthy sense of urgency.

Diversity, Equity, & InclusionWe embrace individuality and know that diverse teams build better products. Our commitment to inclusion across race, gender, age, religion, identity, and background drives our culture and our business forward every day.

Job DetailsWe are seeking a Regional Insurance Product Managerto own state-level strategy and market performance across an assigned region, and to help bring Openly insurance products to independent agents across the country. Reporting to the Director of Insurance Product Management, this highly visible role offers the opportunity to lead key insurance product management initiatives and interact with business leaders across Technology and Operations Teams. This role requires a self-motivated, high-energy individual who can efficiently function in a fast-paced, performance-driven environment.

Key ResponsibilitiesOwning state-level strategy and calibrating Openly''s homeowners program for assigned states and new state entries, including UW eligibility, coverage offerings, competitive positioning, and Openly proprietary models

Managing the state filing process and DOI relationships and correspondence, ensuring timely regulatory approval

Collaborating with our Technology and Operations teams to successfully implement rate reviews and new state launches

Monitoring and analyzing key performance indicators and drivers of profitability, including loss ratios, actuarial indications, frequency/severity trends, sales conversion, persistency, and translating findings into actionable strategic recommendations

Developing cost-benefit analyses of state-level strategic initiatives and presenting recommendations that balance market opportunity with company objectives and profitability targets

Identifying business challenges and opportunities, designing analytical frameworks to evaluate options, and delivering sound recommendations

Cultivating partnerships with Business Development, serving as the primary conduit for field-level market feedback into the Insurance Product organization

Escalating state-level insights that warrant countrywide product changes, acting as an internal advocate for market needs

Contributing to other product management initiatives, such as external data evaluations, market/competitor intelligence, and new product development

Requirements3-5 years of experience in insurance product management or product development roles, with a demonstrated focus on strategy, analytics, or state-level product ownership

A degree in Business Administration, Mathematics, Actuarial Science, Economics, Statistics, or related field

Solid analytical skills with the ability to develop and interpret quantitative analyses and translate findings into strategic narratives for senior business leaders and cross-functional audiences

Demonstrated ability to identify and define complex business problems and develop relevant analytical frameworks to deliver solutions, often operating in ambiguity and leveraging creativity

Strong communication, storytelling, and project management skills

Able to collaborate effectively with people at all levels across the company

Strong decision-making skills, using data to inform strategic recommendations

P&C insurance experience is required, and homeowners insurance experience is a plus

Insurance product compliance and/or state regulatory relationship experience is a plus

Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full‑time basis. This position is not eligible for employer visa sponsorship now or in the future.

Perks & BenefitsGreat work happens when people feel supported, valued, and empowered. From comprehensive health coverage to remote-work flexibility, our benefits are designed to care for you and your family at every stage of life.

Remote-First Culture:We supported remote work long before it became standard, and we remain dedicated to a flexible, distributed team.

Competitive Pay & Equity:Top-tier base salary plus ownership in Openly’s growth.

Comprehensive Health Coverage:Medical, dental, and vision plans tailored to you and your family.

Life & Disability Insurance:Full coverage including voluntary supplemental options.

Parental Leave: Up to 8 weeks (320 hours) of paid parental leave for eligible employees (with additional disability coverage available for birthing parents).

401(k) Company Contribution: Openly contributes 3% of your gross income, regardless of whether you make personal contributions.

Home Office Setup: A $1,500 upfront allowance to build your ideal remote workspace, plus a $75/month internet stipend.

Professional Development: $2,000 annually to invest in courses, conferences, or resources that help you grow.

"Be Well" Program: A $50/month stipend dedicated to your personal health and well-being.

Volunteer Hours & Referral Rewards: Paid time off to give back to your community, plus generous financial rewards for referring great talent.

Note: Select roles may also be eligible for cash incentives or sales commissions. Eligibility for all compensation and benefits is governed by applicable plan terms.

Our Hiring Commitment:We believe interviewing is a two-way street. We’ve designed our hiring process to be transparent, respectful, and human. At every step, you’ll have space to showcase your strengths, ask tough questions, and discover if Openly is the right place for your next chapter.

U.S. Citizens, Green Card Holders, and those authorized to work in the U.S. for any employer and currently residing in the US will be considered.

Openly is committed to equal employment opportunity and non-discrimination for all employees and qualified applicants without regard to a person''s race, color, sex, gender identity or expression, age, religion, national origin, ancestry, ethnicity, disability, veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, marital status, or any characteristic protected under applicable law. Openly is an E-Verify Employer in the United States. Openly will make reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with known disabilities under applicable law.

We strive to provide an exceptional applicant and candidate journey when you engage with us. In an effort to respond to applicants in a timely manner, we leverage AI to organize applications and resumes based on required and applicable skills and experience. To allow our applicants to drive their initial interview experience with us, we may leverage an AI-supported scheduling tool so you can choose when to meet with our team. While AI assists with efficiency, all hiring decisions are made by our team members. Rest assured, your data is protected according to privacy laws and company policies. Contact our recruitment team with any questions about our AI-assisted hiring process.',
    'active', '2026-09-23T06:51:23.452103+00:00', '', 'google_jobs', 'https://himalayas.app/companies/openly/jobs/regional-insurance-product-manager-remote-us-4870456591', TRUE, ARRAY['Product Manager','Remote']::TEXT[]
)
