INSERT INTO jobs (
    company_name, company_logo_url, position_title, location, employment_type,
    salary_min, salary_max, salary_currency, salary_period, description,
    status, posted_at, external_id, source, url, is_remote, tags
) VALUES (
    'Motorola Solutions', 'https://serpapi.com/searches/6ab376d9b24c5d42c30cc8e3/images/OGQHoV2l4Ewofvqi7iLEtnFkRuSOazskWnFcTZMfzYY.jpeg', 'Sr. Product Manager', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Company Overview

At Motorola Solutions, we believe that everything starts with our people. We’re a global close-knit community, united by the relentless pursuit to help keep people safer everywhere. We build and connect technologies to help protect people, property and places. Our solutions foster the collaboration that’s critical for safer communities, safer schools, safer hospitals, safer businesses, and ultimately, safer nations. Connect with a career that matters, and help us build a safer future.

Department Overview

The Evidence Product Management team owns the roadmap for delivering Motorola Solutions’ body cameras, vehicle cameras, and evidence management software. These products are used worldwide to keep communities and individuals safe in public safety and enterprise organizations.

Job Description

We are looking for a passionate Product Development Manager, a problem solver to join the Evidence team.

Responsibilities

Defining Epics features and product roadmapWriting user stories and product requirements driven by customer use cases and product strategyPrioritizing backlog based on inputs from customers, sales, customer support and product strategyIdentifying customer needs and market requirements and using technical skills to create feature and technical requirementsLeveraging deep background experience for working with go-to-market organizations and translating technical feature details into customer-friendly, non-technical messagingBeing a technical liaison between the development team, the customer and customer support teamsEstimating cost of development, operations, and licensing behind features and software that will be soldPlanning and designing development sprint backlog of features to be deliveredIdentifying and mitigating technical risks in feature designStudying user feedback and usage patterns to identify necessary feature changes to increase customer adoption and efficiency

Qualifications

Bachelor''s degree8+ years of experience in Software Development industry with 3+ years of experience in Product Development or a similar roleExcellent communication skills (English)Proven technical and analytical skillsDisplaying leadership, organizational and execution skills 

Target Base Salary Range: $130,000 - $140,000 USD

Consistent with Motorola Solutions values and applicable law, we provide the following information to promote pay transparency and equity. Pay within this range varies and depends on job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. The actual offer will be based on the individual candidate.

Basic Requirements

Bachelor''s degree with 8+ years of experience in Software Development industry with 3+ years of experience in Product Development or a similar role.Legal authorization to work in the U.S. indefinitely is required. Employer work permit sponsorship is not available for this position.

Travel Requirements

Under 10%

Relocation Provided

None

Position Type

Experienced

Referral Payment Plan

Yes

Our U.S. Benefits Include

Incentive Bonus PlansMedical, Dental, Vision benefits401K with Company Match10 Paid HolidaysGenerous Paid Time Off PackagesEmployee Stock Purchase PlanPaid Parental & Family Leaveand more!

EEO Statement

Motorola Solutions is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion or belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status or any other legally-protected characteristic.

We are proud of our people-first and community-focused culture, empowering every Motorolan to be their most authentic self and to do their best work to deliver on the promise of a safer world. If you’d like to join our team but feel that you don’t quite meet all of the preferred skills, we’d still love to hear why you think you’d be a great addition to our team.

We’re committed to providing an inclusive and accessible recruiting experience for candidates with disabilities, or other physical or mental health conditions. To request an accommodation, please complete this Reasonable Accommodations Form so we can assist you.',
    'active', '2026-09-19T06:51:23.452190+00:00', '', 'google_jobs', 'https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/sr-product-manager-at-motorola-solutions-4469522016', TRUE, ARRAY['Product Manager','Remote']::TEXT[]
)
