INSERT INTO jobs (
    company_name, company_logo_url, position_title, location, employment_type,
    salary_min, salary_max, salary_currency, salary_period, description,
    status, posted_at, external_id, source, url, is_remote, tags
) VALUES (
    'Triumph Financial Inc', 'https://serpapi.com/images/i/iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAADgAAAA4CAMAAACfWMssAAAAflBMVEX____7-_vv9vb39_cAf4vx8fEAgYz1-Pm_19rAwMFmZ2t7e39EmqKz0dS7u7xram4AeYUlkZoCiZPm5ubg7O2mztKYwsZhYmeio6V0dXjW5-lsq7Klx8yIuL7o8PJ_srhUoagxMzqEhYhKS1Hb29xUVVrL3-GxsbOXmJrNzc6CHBsVAAAA7klEQVRIie2Ry26DMBBF7_AyxjYUEyCADQ5tSPr_P1gTumjVRRUpSx_Ji9H4-I48QCAQCAReC0UPnhfzt6TWSY04TWOg-dnyNaKInX7df1R7Tp4lbZdIlH1RUnyOiShOkfqHMDQY9WQsGEPEwGZgxuKPUbvoWqs6CXCOy33l55K_i6L4uIrbug4naSCV1LTUm5abc5uMFqnyh2i6bRdLTgKC3zgf0vsnHyBWVOM0e3Gz7eTUMloHSGNrpY5R1T7qt9hc-0PsKy6oGi3gvJg7qexofK5TU30kJpnWmfzzacP_-yBiRM-vIxAIBAKv5AsKqg7OBPwfnAAAAABJRU5ErkJggg.png', 'Staff Product Manager - Freight/Logistics Intelligence (Open to Remote)', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    151038, 234109, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Join Triumph!

At Triumph, our vision is a world where freight transactions are accurate and seamless on the most modern and secure freight transaction network. That''s why we''re looking for passionate, innovative, solutions-oriented people to join our team. We thrive on providing exceptional customer service and we look for team members with an entrepreneurial spirit and a passion to build successful partnerships with our clients. Because at the end of the day our goal is to help our partners businesses run better.

At Triumph, our vision is a world where freight transactions are accurate and seamless on the most modern and secure freight transaction network. That''s why we''re looking for passionate, innovative, solutions-oriented people to join our team. We thrive on providing exceptional customer service and we look for team members with an entrepreneurial spirit and a passion to build successful partnerships with our clients. Because at the end of the day our goal is to help our partners businesses run better.

We''re on the hunt for a dynamic and experienced Staff Product Manager with transportation/freight industry experience to drive high-impact product initiatives and deliver solutions that scale. If you''re passionate about shaping the future of products that solve real customer problems and you thrive in a fast-paced, collaborative environment, this role is for you.

A Day in the Life

As a Staff Product Manager on the Intelligence team, you''ll be at the forefront of shaping our product roadmap. From collaborating with cross-functional teams to launching complex, customer-centric products, you''ll guide every step of the product lifecycle. Your ability to communicate product vision, align teams, and drive decision-making will ensure our products consistently meet and exceed business and customer goals.

Triumph Intelligence is redefining how the transportation industry uses data at scale. With industry-leading pricing solutions and visibility into over 65% of North American brokered truckload freight, we develop intelligence products that power critical market decisions across the freight ecosystem. Our mission is to create efficiencies by bringing network-level insight to freight transactions - unlocking better outcomes for brokers, carriers, and shippers.

What You''ll Be Doing

Lead and communicate the product vision and strategy in alignment with company objectives.

Manage the full product lifecycle from discovery to launch and iteration.

Collaborate closely with software engineers, designers, data, and marketing teams and our customers to deliver high-quality products on time.

Analyze market trends, customer feedback, and product performance to guide decision-making.

Prioritize product features and enhancements based on business impact and customer value.

Mentor and inspire the product team, sharing best practices and helping elevate the team''s capabilities.

Influence key stakeholders, including executives, to align and drive support for product initiatives.

Identify new product opportunities and stay ahead of emerging technologies.

What Makes You a Great Fit

Experience: 7+ years in product management, with at least 2 years in a senior or staff-level role.

Required: Logistics, Transportation, Supply Chain or Data and Analytics (e.g. BI, AI/ML, data platforms or data products).

Expertise: Proven track record of launching successful products in B2B/B2C environments.

Collaboration: Comfortable working with cross-functional teams, including engineers, designers, and marketers.

Technical Background: Strong understanding of technical concepts and agile development processes.

Leadership: Able to mentor, lead teams, and influence stakeholders across all levels.

Skills: Strong communication, strategic thinking, data-driven decision-making, and problem-solving abilities.

Tools: Familiarity with Jira, Confluence, Aha!, Figma, and other product management tools.

Education: Bachelor''s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Business, or a related field (MBA or advanced degree a plus).

Apply Now

