    'AC/DGAL', NULL, 'Directeur de projet Product Manager Réferentiels Outils Transverses', 'Remote', 'Full-time',
    NULL, NULL, 'USD', 'Yearly', 'Product Manager Role The Product Manager is responsible for the coherence, prioritization, and trajectory of its products, in respect of the strategic orientations and arbitrations of the DGAL. They are in charge of designing and sharing the product vision in consultation with the business offices in agreement with the multi-year roadmap. They are responsible for the products of the "Transversal References and Tools" line implementing the SIAL references as well as the transversal tools made available to all the business sub-directions. The portfolio may evolve as well as the priorities depending on the stakes and arbitrations of the DGAL. 

Description of Missions: 

 Define and adapt the product roadmap: define the different versions in consultation with the POs and follow the realization schedules. Manage the life of the products of the product line: this includes all the stages of the product life cycle, from the product investigation phase, definition of the backlog (epic and functionalities) to the product services with the holding of indicators, the follow-up of the realizations and their costs. Share the product vision: the PM ensures the good diffusion of the updated product vision to all stakeholders through an adapted communication plan. Identify the risks related to the development and deployment of the product and propose actions for resolution or mitigation. Dimension the resources: the PM ensures the good allocation of resources to achieve the objectives of the product roadmap.  The PM coordinates the integrated teams of its product line: they are composed of a PO, the business representative, developers, the teachlead, the OPS, the end users and if applicable the technical manager, the business analyst, UX/UI designer. The SIAL is in the process of transformation towards the product mode: the method used varies according to the projects and there are still projects managed in a short V cycle. The position is functionally attached to the program director of the product line and administratively to the BRAVAL. 

Relational Field: Other members of the integrated team, Teams of BRAVAL and DelSIAL, notably the Data team, Cross-functional and business MOA offices of the DGAL, decentralized services, Network of assistance to business users constituted of regional mission managers (COSIR), Teams of Master of Works and service provider AMOA, Institutional and professional partners. 

Profile Sought KNOWLEDGE: Excellent knowledge in the conduct of IT projects (V cycle and product mode / agile) Good technical knowledge Knowledge of the principles of urbanization of information systems Knowledge of business domains would be an asset Knowledge of public procurement would be an asset 

SKILLS: Aptitude for teamwork and team leadership. Collaboration in transversality with diverse stakeholders. Relational and pedagogical qualities. Capacity for analysis and synthesis. Sense of listening and ease in oral and written communication. Regularity and precision in reporting. Force of proposal. 

Minimum Education Level Required  Level 5 Diplomas of level bac +2  Additional Information Contact Person(s): Sylvie LACARELLE Head of office in charge of resources, assistance and valorization of data 01 49 55 83 79 sylvie.lacarelle@agriculture.gouv.fr Léa MARTEL Director of program References & Transversal Tools 06 25 85 93 20 lea.martel@agriculture.gouv.fr Sophie ANDRE Deputy to the Delegated Support to Services - 01 49 55 58 19 sophie.andre@agriculture.gouv.fr 

Special Conditions of Exercise Position open to agents in situations of disability 

Legal Basis Art. L. 332-2 (2°) 

Status of the Position Susceptible of being vacant as of 18/10/2026 

Reference Profession Director / Director of IT Projects',
    'active', '2026-09-19T06:51:23.452642+00:00', '', 'google_jobs', 'https://lensa.com/job-v1/acdgal/remote/product-manager/4cc1fa296f2e0f62d93335a8da8231a8', TRUE, ARRAY['Product Manager','Remote']::TEXT[]
)
